\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh said¦29104 to¦29106 Mosheh¦29108, “Go¦29109 in to¦29110 Far'oh¦29112 and¦29113 tell¦29104 him¦29114: ‘This is what the¦29119 god¦29119 of¦29119 the¦29120 Hebrews¦29120. Yahweh, says¦29117: Let¦29121 my¦29124 people¦29124 go¦29109 \add so\add* they¦29125 can serve¦29125 me¦29125.
\v 2 Certainly if you're¦29133 unwilling to¦29132 release them¦29132 and¦29133 if you¦29133 keep¦29134 holding¦29134 onto them¦29135,
\v 3 then listen. Yahweh¦29140 is¦29141 about¦29141 to¦29141 \add inflict\add* a¦29150 very¦29152 serious \add ≈deadly disease\add* onto your¦29142 livestock¦29142 which¦29143 are in¦29142 the¦29144 fields¦29144—on¦29145 the horses¦29145, the donkeys¦29146, the camels¦29147, the cattle¦29148, and¦29149 on¦29149 the flock¦29149.
\v 4 \add But\add* Yahweh¦29155 will¦29154 distinguish¦29154 between¦29156 the livestock¦29157 of the Israelis and¦29154 the Egyptians—none of¦29157 the¦29160 Israelis' animals will¦29163 die¦29163.’ ”
\v 5 Then¦29170 Yahweh \add said when it would happen\add*, “Yahweh will¦29175 do¦29175 this¦29178 \add to Egypt\add* tomorrow¦29174.”
\p
\v 6 \add So\add* the next¦29187 day¦29187 Yahweh¦29182 did¦29181 \add what he'd said\add* and¦29181 all¦29189 of¦29189 the¦29190 livestock¦29190 of¦29190 the Egyptians¦29191 died, yet none at all from¦29187 the livestock¦29192 of¦29192 the¦29193 Israelis¦29195 died¦29198.
\v 7 Far'oh sent¦29201 \add people to investigate\add*, and¦29203 wow, not¦29204 even one¦29211 of the livestock¦29207 of¦29207 the¦29207 Israelis¦29208 had¦29206 died¦29206. \add But\add* Far'oh was¦29212 strong-willed and¦29215 wouldn't let¦29216 the¦29219 people¦29219 go¦29216.
\s1 Plague 6: Boils
\rem /s1 The Plague of Boils; The Sixth Plague: Boils; A Plague of Boils
\p
\v 8 Then Yahweh¦29223 told¦29222 Mosheh and¦29222 Aharon¦29229, “Take¦29230 handfuls of ash out of a¦29235 furnace¦29235, then Mosheh¦29237 should \add toss it up in the air in front\add* of¦29239 Far'oh¦29240.
\v 9 It¦29242 will become a powder over all Egypt and then¦29242 it¦29249 will turn into¦29243 boils¦29256—bursting¦29257 blisters¦29258—on people¦29252 and¦29253 on¦29253 animals all¦29259 over Egypt.”
\v 10 \add So\add* they¦29264 took¦29264 some ash from a furnace¦29268, and¦29269 standing¦29269 in¦29280 front¦29270 of¦29267 Far'oh¦29271, Mosheh¦29274 \add tossed it up into the air\add* and¦29276 it¦29276 turned into boils¦29277 with¦29280 bursting¦29279 blisters¦29278 on¦29280 the people¦29280 and¦29281 the animals.\x + \xo 9:10: \xt Rev 16:2.\x*
\v 11 Because¦29292 of¦29288 the boils, the sorcerers weren't \add even\add* able¦29285 to¦29287 stand¦29287 \add there with\add* Mosheh¦29289 because¦29292 the¦29295 sorcerers \add suffered with them\add* along with all¦29297 the Egyptians¦29299.
\v 12 \add But\add* Yahweh caused¦29301 Far'oh¦29306 to remain stubborn and¦29301 he¦29311 didn't¦29307 listen¦29308 to¦29309 them¦29309, just¦29310 as¦29310 Yahweh had¦29311 told¦29311 Mosheh¦29315 \add previously\add*.
\s1 Plague 7: Hail
\rem /s1 A Plague of Hail; The Seventh Plague: Thunder and Hail; The Plague of Hail
\p
\v 13 Then Yahweh told¦29318 Mosheh¦29322, “Get up early¦29323 in¦29324 the morning¦29324, and¦29325 stand in¦29326 front¦29326 of¦29326 Far'oh¦29327 and¦29328 say¦29328 to¦29329 him¦29329, ‘This is what Yahweh, the¦29334 god¦29334 of¦29334 the¦29335 Hebrews¦29335, says¦29332: Let¦29336 my¦29339 people¦29339 go¦29336 so¦29340 they¦29340 can serve¦29340 me¦29340
\v 14 because¦29360 this¦29345 time¦29344, I'm¦29346 about¦29347 to¦29347 send¦29347 all¦29350 my¦29352 plagues¦29352 to¦29353 you and your servants¦29356, and your people¦29357. \add You'll all be deeply distressed by them\add*, in¦29358 order that you¦29359 might¦29359 know¦29359 that¦29360 there¦29361 is¦29361 no \add one else\add* like¦29362 me¦29362 in¦29363 all¦29363 the¦29365 world¦29365.
\v 15 \add By this time\add*, I¦29369 could have reached¦29369 out¦29369 and¦29373 struck¦29373 you¦29374 and¦29375 your¦29377 people¦29377 with¦29378 such \add ≈deadly disease or destruction¦29379\add* that you would all have been¦29379 obliterated from¦29380 the¦29382 land¦29382.
\v 16 However, I've¦29387 kept you for this¦29386 reason¦29387: to show¦29389 you¦29389 my power¦29392 and¦29384 in¦29385 order to proclaim my¦29392 name¦29395 all¦29396 over the¦29398 world¦29398.\x + \xo 9:16: \xt Rom 9:17.\x*
\v 17 You're still¦29400 considering yourself¦29401 to be¦29401 greater than my¦29402 people¦29402 by failing to release them¦29404.
\v 18 \add Now\add* listen¦29406: I'm¦29406 about¦29407 to¦29407 cause extremely heavy¦29411 hail¦29410 to rain¦29407 \add down\add* at¦29418 this time¦29408 tomorrow¦29409. \add It'll be hail like\add* which¦29413 has¦29416 never been¦29416 \add seen before\add* in¦29418 Egypt¦29418 from¦29419 the¦29421 day¦29421 it¦29422 was¦29422 founded¦29422 until now¦29425.
\v 19 \add So\add* send¦29428 for¦29437 your¦29432 livestock¦29432 and everything you own in the country now¦29427, and bring¦29429 it¦29445 in¦29446 under cover because the hail¦29452 will come¦29450 down¦29450 on¦29446 every person and animal¦29442 that¦29443 is¦29445 found¦29445 in the countryside¦29438 and not¦29447 \add sheltering under a roof\add*, and they¦29453 will¦29453 die¦29453.’ ”
\v 20 Some of¦29458 Far'oh's¦29461 servants¦29465 who believed what Yahweh¦29459 said, quickly brought their slaves and¦29466 their livestock¦29468 back into¦29469 their houses¦29471,
\v 21 but¦29473 those \add people\add* who didn't¦29474 believe Yahweh¦29481 \add just\add* left¦29482 their slaves and¦29473 their animals¦29488 out in¦29489 the¦29480 countryside¦29489.
\p
\v 22 “Raise your¦29500 arm up toward the¦29503 sky¦29503,” Yahweh¦29493 told¦29492 Mosheh¦29496, “and¦29504 hail¦29505 \add will strike\add* all¦29506 over Egypt¦29509—on¦29510 the¦29512 people¦29512 and¦29513 animals and¦29516 on¦29516 every¦29517 plant in¦29521 the Egyptian¦29522 countryside¦29520.”
\v 23 \add So\add* Mosheh¦29525 lifted his¦29528 staff¦29528 to¦29529 the¦29531 sky¦29531, and¦29532 Yahweh sent thunder¦29534 and¦29535 hail¦29535, and \add lightning caused fires\add* on¦29542 the¦29544 land¦29544, and \add so\add* Yahweh rained¦29539 hail¦29541 \add down\add* onto Egypt¦29545.
\v 24 There was hail, and¦29547 \add also\add* fire¦29549 coming \add down\add* in¦29551 the¦29551 middle¦29551 of¦29552 the¦29552 hail¦29552. It¦29558 was very¦29554 heavy¦29553, such as¦29559 had¦29558 never been¦29558 in¦29560 all¦29560 of¦29562 Egypt¦29563 since¦29564 it¦29565 became¦29565 a nation¦29566.\x + \xo 9:24: \xt Rev 8:7; 16:21.\x*
\v 25 The¦29569 hail¦29569 struck everything in¦29570 Egypt¦29573—everything that¦29577 was in¦29578 the¦29578 countryside, from¦29579 people¦29579 to¦29580 animals¦29582. \add It also\add* struck every plant and¦29568 broke every¦29592 tree¦29594 \add out\add* in the¦29595 countryside.
\v 26 Only¦29598 in¦29599 the Goshen¦29600 region¦29599 where¦29601 the¦29604 Israelis¦29605 were¦29603, was¦29607 there¦29603 no hail¦29608.
\p
\v 27 Then¦29610 Far'oh¦29611 sent¦29610 for Mosheh¦29613 and¦29614 Aharon¦29614 and¦29615 told¦29615 them¦29616, “I've¦29617 sinned¦29617 this¦29618 time¦29618. Yahweh¦29619 is¦29620 righteous¦29620, and¦29621 me and¦29622 my¦29622 people¦29622 are¦29623 guilty¦29623.
\v 28 Pray¦29625 to¦29626 Yahweh¦29628 \add to stop it,\add* because¦29630 the¦29631 thunder¦29631 of¦29631 God¦29632 and¦29629 hail¦29633 are too much. Then I'll¦29634 release you all—you won't¦29636 have to¦29638 remain \add here\add*.”
\p
\v 29 “As¦29643 I'm leaving¦29643 the¦29646 city¦29646,” Mosheh¦29642 \add ≈replied¦29640\add*, “I'll¦29647 spread¦29647 my¦29650 palms¦29650 \add out\add* to¦29651 Yahweh. The¦29654 thunder¦29654 will¦29655 stop¦29655 and¦29640 the¦29656 hail¦29656 won't¦29657 continue so¦29661 that¦29661 you¦29662 \add will be able to see\add* that¦29663 the¦29665 earth¦29665 belongs to Yahweh.
\v 30 \add But as for\add* you and¦29668 your¦29668 servants¦29668, I¦29669 know¦29669 that¦29670 you still don't¦29671 fear¦29672 Yahweh¦29674 God¦29675.”
\p
