\v 31 \add @Far'oh¦31189\add* called¦31181 for Mosheh¦31182 and¦31183 Aharon¦31183 in the night¦31184 and¦31185 told¦31185 \add <them\add*, “Pack up and get out¦31187 from¦31188 among¦31188 my¦31189 people—you \add two\add* and all the other Israelis¦31196. Go¦31197 and serve¦31198 Yahweh¦31201 as¦31202 you've said¦31202.
\v 32 Also¦31215 take¦31210 your flocks¦31206 and your herds¦31209 as¦31211 you've said¦31212, and¦31213 go¦31213. And¦31214 bless¦31214 me¦31217 as well¦31207.
\rem /s1 The Exodus: From Rameses to Succoth
\p
\v 33 The¦31223 Egyptians urged¦31219 the \add @Israelis¦31223\add*, hurrying¦31224 to¦31232 let them¦31225 go from¦31226 the¦31228 land¦31228 because¦31229 they¦31230 said¦31230, “We're all¦31231 dying¦31232.”
\p
\v 34 \add So\add* the¦31235 people¦31235 carried¦31234 their \add bread\add* dough¦31238 before¦31239 it¦31240 \add ≈could rise\add*. Their¦31236 bread-making bowls¦31241 were¦31242 wrapped in¦31243 their clothes¦31243 on¦31243 their¦31243 shoulders¦31246.
\p
\v 35 The¦31248 Israelis¦31250 did¦31251 everything that Mosheh¦31253 had instructed them, \add including\add* asking¦31254 for items of¦31250 gold¦31260 and silver¦31258, and clothing¦31261 from¦31255 the¦31252 Egyptians¦31255.\x + \xo 12:35-36: \xt Exo 3:21-22.\x*
\v 36 Yahweh¦31263 gave¦31264 the people¦31268 favour¦31267 in¦31269 the eyes¦31269 of¦31269 the¦31271 Egyptians, \add so by\add* their requests¦31271, they¦31272 were able to strip the Egyptians of their wealth.
\rem /s1 The Israelites Leave Egypt; The exodus from Egypt
\p
\v 37 Then the¦31279 Israelis¦31281 walked from¦31282 Rameses¦31282 toward Succoth¦31283—about¦31284 600,000 strong men¦31289 on foot¦31288, not counting \add women and\add* children¦31291.
\v 38 A large assortment of other people also¦31293 went¦31297 with¦31298 them¦31298, along with large numbers of sheep¦31299 and goats, and cattle¦31300.
\p
\v 39 They¦31305 baked¦31305 the¦31308 dough¦31308 that¦31309 they¦31310 brought¦31310 from¦31311 Egypt¦31311 into flat bread¦31312 since it¦31316 \add ≈hadn't had time to rise\add*,\f + \fr 12:39 \ft Most modern readers probably visualise yeast bought from a supermarket when ‘leaven’ (or even ‘yeast’) is mentioned in a Bible translation. However, it's much more likely that each day, a portion of the bread dough was set aside for the natural yeasts (think ‘sour dough’ bread) to accumulate, and then mixed into the new batch of dough the next day and left for the natural yeasts to work and rise the dough. The text here implies that it's possible that the Hebrew word translated ‘unleavened’ really meant ‘unrisen’ on that first ‘pass-over’ night.\f* because¦31314 they¦31319 were¦31319 driven¦31319 out¦31319 of Egypt \add ≈in a hurry\add* and¦31305 hadn't \add ≈had¦31310 time to prepare food¦31312 to take\add*.
\p
\v 40 The¦31332 descendants of¦31332 Yisra'el¦31334 \add !(Yacob¦31334)\add* had lived¦31332 in¦31337 Egypt¦31337 for 430 years¦31339\x + \xo 12:40: \xt Gen 15:13; Gal 3:17.\x*
\v 41 to the day¦31353, because that¦31354 very day was¦31351 when all¦31356 the \add various\add* divisions of¦31352 Yahweh's¦31359 \add people\add* left¦31355 Egypt¦31361.
\v 42 It¦31365 was¦31363 a \add time\add* when they stayed awake all¦31376 night as Yahweh¦31366 took¦31367 them¦31367 out¦31367 of¦31368 Egypt¦31369—a night¦31372 to¦31374 be¦31375 observed in that¦31373 same way by every¦31376 future generation¦31380.
\s1 Instructions for observing the ‘pass-over’
\rem /s1 Instructions for the Passover; Passover Restrictions; Directions for the Passover; Regulations about Passover
\p
\v 43 Then Yahweh¦31384 told¦31383 Mosheh¦31387 and¦31383 Aharon¦31388, “This¦31389 is¦31390 the¦31390 statute¦31390 of¦31390 the¦31391 ‘pass-over¦31391’: No foreigners¦31396 may \add share in\add* the meal \add that night\add*,
\v 44 unless it's¦31410 a slave¦31404 that you¦31409 bought¦31406 and¦31409 who's been circumcised¦31409—
\v 45 no foreigner¦31415 or hired¦31416 helper can \add join in\add* the meal.
\v 46 \add Each animal\add* must¦31425 be¦31425 eaten¦31425 in¦31423 only one¦31424 house—don't take¦31428 any¦31432 of¦31432 the¦31434 meat¦31434 outside¦31435. And¦31436 don't break¦31438 any of the animals bones¦31436.\x + \xo 12:46: \xt Num 9:12; Yhn 19:36.\x*
\v 47 Every¦31445 Israeli¦31444 must¦31446 observe it¦31447,
\v 48 and¦31449 if someone is living¦31451 among you¦31452 and¦31454 wants to¦31456 join in Yahweh's¦31456 ‘pass-over¦31455’, then every¦31459 male¦31461 in their family must¦31451 be circumcised¦31457. Only then will¦31457 they be allowed to observe¦31464 it¦31464, and¦31465 then they should be¦31465 considered like¦31466 a native¦31466 of¦31466 the¦31467 land¦31467. No uncircumcised¦31470 person¦31470 may eat¦31473 it¦31474.
\v 49 This one¦31477 law¦31476 will¦31478 apply to¦31479 both the natives¦31479, and¦31480 those who¦31481 live¦31481 among¦31482 you¦31482 all.”
\v 50 All¦31492 the¦31487 Israelis¦31488 followed those instructions¦31490 that Yahweh¦31491 had¦31490 given through Mosheh¦31494 and¦31495 Aharon¦31497,
\v 51 and¦31502 \add so\add* on¦31503 that¦31505 very day¦31504, Yahweh¦31507 took¦31506 all the¦31503 Israelis¦31511 out¦31506 of¦31503 Egypt¦31513 \add grouped\add* by their¦31516 \add family\add* divisions.
\c 13
\s1 God owns the first child
