\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦31520 told¦31524 Mosheh¦31523,
\v 2 “All¦31537 firstborn¦31531 \add offspring\add* are to be consecrated¦31526 to¦31528 me¦31528—the first¦31531 product of¦31532 every¦31533 womb¦31535, whether human¦31538 or animal, belongs to¦31540 me¦31540.”\x + \xo 13:2: \xt Num 3:13; Luk 2:23.\x*
\s1 The ‘Flat Bread Celebration’
\rem /s1 The Festival of Unleavened Bread
\p
\v 3 Then¦31543 Mosheh¦31544 told¦31543 the¦31547 people¦31547, “\add Always\add* remember¦31548 this day¦31551, that¦31552 you went¦31554 out¦31554 of¦31556 Egypt¦31555, \add rescued\add* from¦31556 slavery¦31557, because¦31558 Yahweh¦31562 \add ≈used his power¦31559\add* to¦31545 bring¦31561 you out¦31561 from¦31564 there¦31564. And¦31565 \add ≈nothing with¦31559 yeast in¦31559 it¦31566\add* can be¦31566 eaten¦31566 \add when you celebrate this\add*.
\v 4 Today you¦31570 are¦31571 leaving¦31571 in¦31572 the¦31572 month¦31572 of¦31572 Aviv¦31573,
\v 5 and¦31575 \add when\add* Yahweh¦31579 brings¦31578 you¦31578 into¦31580 the¦31582 \add ≈area occupied by\add* the¦31583 Canaanites¦31583, Hittites¦31584, Amorites¦31585, Hivites¦31586, and¦31587 the¦31587 Yebusites¦31587 (which¦31588 he¦31589 swore¦31589 to¦31590 your¦31590 fathers¦31590 to¦31591 give¦31591 to¦31592 you—a land¦31593 flowing¦31594 with¦31602 milk¦31595 and¦31596 honey¦31596) you must¦31578 observe¦31597 this ceremony¦31600 in¦31602 this \add same\add* month¦31602.
\v 6 You¦31607 must¦31607 eat¦31607 \add only\add* flat¦31608 bread¦31608 for¦31612 seven¦31610 days¦31606, and¦31609 then on¦31609 the¦31609 seventh¦31610 day¦31609, there will¦31607 be a festival¦31611 to¦31612 \add honour\add* Yahweh¦31612.
\v 7 \add Again,\add* you must only eat¦31615 flat bread for¦31622 seven¦31617 days¦31618—\add not only that\add* you mustn't \add even have\add* any risen bread, nor must you have any yeast within any of¦31631 your¦31631 borders¦31631.
\v 8 On that¦31636 \add festival\add* day¦31635, you¦31633 must¦31633 tell¦31633 your¦31634 \add children\add*, ‘This is because of¦31638 what¦31639 Yahweh¦31641 did¦31640 for \add us\add* when¦31643 \add we left\add* Egypt¦31644.’
\v 9 It'll¦31664 be¦31656 \add ≈like a reminder¦31652 written\add* on your hand¦31661 and¦31646 \add ≈hanging from¦31665 your forehead\add*, so¦31655 that¦31655 \add ≈you'll remember to pass on\add* Yahweh's¦31658 instructions¦31657 because¦31660 \add *he¦31663\add* \add ≈used his power\add* to bring¦31663 you¦31663 out¦31663 of¦31651 Egypt¦31665.
\v 10 \add So\add* you¦31667 must¦31667 \add ≈follow those instructions\add* at the¦31670 appointed¦31672 time¦31672 \add ≈year after year\add*.
\s1 Offering up the oldest children
\rem /s1 The Consecration of the Firstborn; The First-Born
\p
\v 11 Later¦31678, when Yahweh¦31681 brings¦31680 you¦31680 into¦31682 the¦31684 land¦31684 of¦31684 the¦31685 Canaanites¦31685 as¦31686 he¦31687 promised¦31687 to¦31688 you and¦31689 your¦31689 ancestors¦31689, and¦31690 he¦31690 gives¦31690 it¦31690 to¦31691 you,
\v 12 then¦31693 hand over to Yahweh all¦31694 \add your\add* oldest¦31696 \add ≈sons\add*, and¦31700 all¦31700 the¦31704 oldest, male¦31709 animal offspring that¦31706 are yours¦31708. They will¦31707 \add then\add* belong¦31707 to Yahweh.\x + \xo 13:12: \xt Exo 34:19-20; Luk 2:23.\x*
\v 13 In the case of¦31714 the oldest donkey¦31715 foal, you¦31716 must buy it back \add by killing a lamb\add* instead of it. If¦31718 you don't¦31720 buy it back, you must kill the donkey by breaking¦31722 its¦31722 neck¦31722. You¦31727 \em must\em* buy back every¦31723 one of your¦31726 oldest sons¦31726,
\v 14 and¦31729 \add ≈in¦31734 the future¦31734\add* when your¦31733 son¦31733 asks¦31732 you¦31732, ‘What's¦31736 that¦31738 about¦31733?’ then¦31729 you must¦31732 tell him¦31740, ‘\add ≈We were enslaved in Egypt¦31745, but¦31729 Yahweh¦31744 used his incredible power¦31741\add* to¦31735 bring¦31743 us¦31743 out¦31743.
\v 15 And¦31749 so¦31770 it¦31749 was¦31749 that when Far'oh¦31753 was too stubborn¦31752 to¦31754 let¦31754 us¦31754 go¦31754, then¦31749 Yahweh struck all¦31757 of¦31757 the¦31762 oldest¦31762 sons and¦31764 oldest male¦31778 animals¦31767 in¦31760 Egypt¦31761. That's why \add we\add* offer all the¦31766 oldest¦31766 offspring to¦31773 Yahweh, and¦31779 why \add we need to buy back\add* all¦31779 our oldest¦31781 sons¦31782.’
\v 16 \add So\add* you must place a reminder on your hand¦31789 and¦31785 hanging on your forehead that Yahweh¦31797 used his incredible power¦31794 to bring¦31796 us¦31796 out¦31796 of¦31792 Egypt¦31798.”
\s1 Led by cloud and fire
