\p
\v 17 When¦31802 Far'oh¦31803 released the¦31806 people¦31806, God¦31810 didn't¦31807 lead¦31809 them¦31809 through the \add ≈area occupied by\add* the Philistines¦31813, although \add @that¦31811 way¦31811\add* was¦31815 shorter, because¦31814 \add *he¦31819\add* said¦31819, “\add ≈It's¦31801 best if¦31814 the people don't¦31807 have to face¦31825 war immediately, or they¦31825 might change their minds\add* and¦31827 \add then want to\add* return¦31827 to Egypt¦31828.”
\v 18 \add So\add* God¦31831 caused¦31830 the¦31835 people¦31835 to¦31830 take the¦31836 path¦31836 going towards the¦31837 wilderness¦31837 and¦31830 the¦31838 Red Sea¦31838.\f + \fr 13:18 \ft Probably towards the \+em Gulf of Suez\+em*: see https://armstronginstitute.org/339-where-did-the-red-sea-crossing-take-place.\f* The¦31843 Israeli¦31845 left¦31842 Egypt¦31847 \add ≈in formation as if ready for¦31841 battle¦31841\add*.
