\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦31913 told¦31917 Mosheh¦31916,
\v 2 “Tell the¦31922 Israelis¦31923 that¦31924 they¦31924 should¦31924 turn¦31924 and¦31925 camp in¦31926 front¦31926 of¦31926 Pi¦31927-Hahirot¦31928, between¦31929 Migdol¦31930 and¦31931 the¦31932 sea, in¦31933 front¦31933 of¦31933 Baal¦31934-Zephon¦31935. You all are to¦31920 camp by the¦31926 sea opposite¦31936 it¦31936.
\v 3 Then¦31942 Far'oh¦31943 will¦31946 say¦31942, ‘They¦31945 are¦31946 confused¦31946 \add and lost\add*—the wilderness¦31951 has¦31949 boxed them¦31950 in¦31946.’
\v 4 I'll strengthen¦31953 Far'oh's¦31958 \add ≈resolve\add* and¦31959 he'll¦31959 chase¦31959 after¦31960 them¦31960. Then¦31953 because¦31968 of¦31965 Far'oh¦31962 and¦31963 all¦31963 his¦31965 army¦31965, I'll be \add honoured\add* and¦31966 the Egyptians¦31967 will¦31966 know¦31966 that¦31968 I¦31961 am¦31971 Yahweh¦31971.” \add ≈So¦31953 the¦31956 Israelis camped where they¦31972 were instructed\add*.
\rem /s1 The Egyptians Pursue Israel
\p
\v 5 When¦31976 the¦31977 king¦31977 of¦31977 Egypt¦31978 was¦31982 told¦31976 that¦31992 the Israelis¦31981 had¦31980 fled¦31980, \add *he¦31984\add* and¦31985 his¦31985 servants¦31985 \add started thinking about their own\add* people¦31988 and¦31989 they¦31989 asked¦31989, “What¦31990 have¦31993 we¦31993 done¦31993 by letting¦31996 the Israeli slaves go¦31996 free?”
\v 6 Then¦32002 he¦32009 hitched¦32002 up his chariot¦32005 and¦32006 took¦32009 his \add army\add* with¦32010 him¦32010.
\v 7 He¦32012 took¦32012 600 of¦32019 the best chariots as well as all¦32018 the¦32019 other Egyptian¦32020 chariots and¦32012 officers¦32021 \add to supervise\add* them.
\v 8 Yahweh¦32027 strengthened the Egyptian¦32039 king's¦32032 resolve and¦32026 so Far'oh¦32031 pursued¦32034 after¦32035 the¦32036 Israelis¦32037 after they had confidently marched¦32040 out¦32040 \add of Egypt\add*.
\v 9 The¦32052 Egyptians pursued¦32044 them, then¦32044 all¦32053 of¦32053 Far'oh's¦32057 horses¦32055 and chariots¦32056, along with his mounted soldiers and his foot army¦32059, overtook¦32047 them¦32048 camping¦32049 above the¦32064 sea¦32052 above Pi¦32062-Hahirot¦32063, across from Baal¦32065-Zephon¦32066.
\p
\v 10 As \add the Egyptians\add* approached¦32069, the¦32071 Israelis¦32073 looked back, and¦32077 \add to their horror\add*, saw¦32077 the army coming¦32069 after¦32081 them¦32081. They¦32082 were¦32082 extremely afraid¦32082 and¦32084 cried¦32084 out¦32084 to¦32088 Yahweh¦32090.
\v 11 They¦32092 \add complained\add* to¦32093 Mosheh¦32095, “Is¦32097 it because¦32096 there¦32097 weren't¦32097 any graves¦32099 in¦32100 Egypt¦32100 that¦32106 you brought¦32101 us¦32101 here to¦32102 die¦32102 in¦32103 the wilderness¦32103? What¦32104 have¦32107 you¦32107 done¦32107 to us? Why did¦32107 you bring¦32109 us¦32109 out¦32109 from¦32110 Egypt?
\v 12 Isn't this¦32114 \add exactly what we told\add* you¦32118 in¦32119 Egypt¦32119 when we said¦32120, ‘\add ≈Just leave us alone\add* and let us serve¦32123 the Egyptians’? Because¦32127 serving¦32130 the Egyptians \add sounds a lot\add* better¦32128 to¦32129 us¦32129 than¦32134 dying¦32134 \add out here\add* in¦32135 the wilderness¦32135.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦32137 Mosheh¦32138 told¦32137 the¦32141 people¦32141, “You mustn't be¦32144 afraid¦32144. Stand¦32145 still and¦32137 see¦32146 how Yahweh¦32150 saves you all—he's¦32153 going to¦32154 do¦32142 it¦32137 today, because¦32156 any Egyptians that¦32151 you see¦32158 today, you'll never, ever see¦32165 them¦32165 again¦32166.
\v 14 Yahweh¦32171 himself will¦32172 fight¦32172 for¦32173 you all—all you need to do is to remain calm¦32175.”
\rem /s1 Escape through the Red Sea
\v 15 Then Yahweh¦32179 \add scolded\add* Mosheh¦32182, “Why¦32183 are¦32185 you¦32185 \add still here\add* crying¦32185 out¦32185 to¦32186 me¦32186? Talk to¦32188 the¦32190 Israelis¦32192 and¦32178 get them moving forward¦32193.
\v 16 As for you, raise¦32196 your staff¦32199 and¦32200 stretch¦32200 your arm out¦32200 over¦32204 the¦32206 sea¦32206 and¦32207 divide¦32207 it¦32207. Then¦32195 the¦32209 Israelis¦32211 will go¦32208 on¦32214 onto dry ground¦32214 through the middle¦32212 of¦32209 the sea¦32213.
\v 17 \add Yes, watch me!\add* I'll strengthen¦32218 the¦32221 resolve of¦32221 the Egyptians and¦32223 they'll¦32223 enter \add between the sea\add* after¦32224 them¦32224. Then¦32216 I'll be¦32218 honoured¦32225 because of \add what will happen to\add* Far'oh¦32226 and¦32227 all¦32227 his army¦32229, and his¦32229 chariots¦32230 and his horsemen¦32231.
\v 18 ⇔The honour¦32239 that I¦32239 gain¦32239 \add ≈through¦32240 that will¦32233 cause\add* the Egyptians to know¦32233 that¦32235 I'm¦32237 Yahweh¦32238.”
\p
\v 19 Then¦32244 God's¦32246 messenger¦32245 who¦32247 travelled¦32251 ahead of the Israelis¦32250, moved and¦32251 went¦32251 behind¦32252 them. \add Also\add* the¦32254 pillar¦32254 of cloud¦32255 moved from¦32256 in¦32248 front¦32248 of them and stood¦32257 behind¦32258 them¦32258
\v 20 and \add so\add* it was¦32268 then¦32260 between¦32261 the¦32263 \add coming\add* Egyptians and¦32265 the¦32266 Israelis¦32267. Then¦32260 the¦32269 cloud¦32269 became darkness¦32270 \add on the Egyptian side\add*, \add yet it lit up the other side\add*, and no one could approach¦32277 it all¦32282 night¦32284.
\v 21 Then¦32286 Mosheh¦32287 stretched¦32286 his¦32290 arm out¦32286 over¦32291 the¦32293 sea¦32293 and¦32294 Yahweh¦32295 sent a¦32300 strong¦32302 east¦32301 wind¦32301. It¦32306 blew all¦32303 night¦32305 and divided¦32311 the sea \add on each side\add* and dried the \add strip of\add* land¦32310 in¦32300 the middle.
\v 22 \add So\add* then¦32314 the¦32315 Israelis¦32317 entered through the¦32318 middle¦32318 of the¦32319 sea¦32319 on¦32320 dry ground¦32320 with¦32320 a wall¦32323 of water¦32321 on each side of them.\x + \xo 14:22: \xt 1Cor 10:1-2; Heb 11:29.\x*
\v 23 \add However,\add* the Egyptians pursued¦32327 after¦32330 them¦32330. Every¦32331 one of Far'oh's¦32333 horses¦32332 and chariots¦32334 and¦32335 his¦32335 horsemen¦32335 \add also\add* entered into¦32336 the¦32338 middle¦32338 of¦32338 the¦32339 sea¦32339.
\v 24 \add By now morning was coming\add* and Yahweh¦32345 looked¦32344 down¦32344 through the¦32348 pillar¦32350 of¦32348 fire¦32351 and¦32352 cloud¦32352, and¦32353 he¦32353 caused confusion¦32353 for the¦32355 Egyptian¦32356 army.
\v 25 He¦32358 caused¦32358 the¦32360 wheels¦32360 of¦32360 their¦32361 chariots¦32361 to turn¦32358 unevenly \add so they became difficult\add* to¦32362 drive¦32362, and¦32364 the Egyptians \add complained\add*, “Let's¦32366 retreat¦32358 from¦32367 \add following\add* the Israelis¦32367, because¦32369 Yahweh¦32370 is¦32371 fighting¦32371 against¦32373 Egypt¦32365 and for¦32372 them¦32372.”
\rem /s1 The Pursuers Drowned
\p
\v 26 \add On the other side,\add* Yahweh¦32377 told¦32376 Mosheh¦32380, “Stretch¦32381 your¦32384 arm out¦32381 over¦32385 the¦32387 sea¦32387 and the¦32389 waters¦32389 will \add flow back\add* onto the Egyptians and onto \add @Far'oh's¦32388\add* chariots¦32395 and¦32396 his horsemen¦32398.”
\v 27 \add So\add* Mosheh¦32401 stretched¦32400 his¦32404 arm out¦32400 over¦32405 the sea¦32407, and¦32408 as the day broke, the sea began to return¦32408 to its¦32412 normal¦32412 place. The¦32407 Egyptians \add turned and\add* fled¦32414 before¦32415 its impact \add but\add* Yahweh¦32417 shook¦32416 the Egyptians \add off their horses and chariots\add* in¦32421 the¦32421 middle¦32421 of¦32412 the¦32422 sea¦32422.
\v 28 \add So\add* the sea returned¦32424 and¦32426 covered¦32426 the¦32429 chariots¦32429 and¦32430 the¦32432 horsemen¦32432—even Far'oh's¦32435 entire army¦32434 that had entered into the¦32436 sea after¦32437 \add @the¦32424 Israelis¦32424\add*. Not¦32439 even one¦32445 of¦32434 \add @the¦32424 pursuers¦32424\add* remained¦32441.
\v 29 \add But\add* the¦32447 \add ≈Israelis¦32448\add* had walked¦32449 through the¦32451 middle¦32451 of the¦32452 sea¦32452 on dry ground¦32450 with¦32450 a wall¦32455 of water¦32453 \add ≈on each side of them¦32454\add*.
\p
\v 30 \add So\add* Yahweh¦32460 saved¦32459 Yisrael¦32465 from¦32466 Egypt's¦32467 power that¦32462 day¦32461, and¦32459 the Israelis¦32469 saw¦32468 the Egyptians' bodies \add washed up\add* on¦32474 the¦32476 shore¦32476.
\v 31 \add All\add* \add ≈the Israelis¦32480\add* saw¦32479 the¦32483 \add ≈incredible power¦32483\add* that¦32485 Yahweh had¦32486 used against the Egyptians, and¦32489 the¦32490 people¦32490 revered¦32489 Yahweh, and¦32494 put their trust¦32494 in¦32488 him and¦32496 his¦32497 servant¦32497 Mosheh¦32496.
\c 15
