\p
\v 1 Then God¦34848 \add ≈gave these¦34853 instructions\add* \add to the Israelis\add*:
\v 2 I'm¦34857 your¦34860 god¦34860 Yahweh¦34859, who¦34862 \add ≈rescued you¦34863\add*\f + \fr 20:2 \ft Although modern English doesn't easily distinguish it, this discourse is addressed to singular ‘you’, i.e., to the Israelis as one group. While some of our modern, individualistic cultures might naturally interpret these rules as applying to individuals, they were given to Yisrael/Israel to implement at a national level.\f* \add ≈from¦34864 where you were¦34859 enslaved in\add* Egypt¦34865.
\li1
\v 3 You mustn't own any other¦34879 gods¦34877 \add ≈in my¦34883 sight\add*.
\li1
\v 4 You¦34888 mustn't make¦34888 a carved figure for¦34890 yourself¦34890, nor \add carve a copy\add* of anything in¦34901 the sky¦34901 above¦34903 or in the¦34907 earth¦34907 below¦34909, or that's¦34912 in¦34914 the water¦34914 under¦34916 the earth¦34918.\x + \xo 20:4-5: \xt Exo 34:17; Lev 19:4; 26:1; Deu 4:15-18; 27:15.\x*
\v 5 Don't¦34922 bow¦34924 down¦34924 to¦34927 \add @idols¦34927\add* and don't¦34922 serve¦34930 them¦34930, because¦34932 I, your¦34935 god¦34935 Yahweh¦34934, am¦34936 a jealous¦34937 God¦34935. I remember the sins of the fathers¦34940 and \add punish\add* the children¦34943 of \add even\add* the third¦34946 and¦34947 fourth¦34949 \add generation\add* of¦34950 those¦34950 who¦34950 hate¦34950 me¦34950,\x + \xo 20:5-6: \xt Exo 34:6-7; Num 14:18; Deu 7:9-10.\x*
\v 6 \add but\add* I \add ≈faithfully fulfil my promises\add* to¦34957 \em thousands¦34957\em* \add of generations\add* of¦34959 those¦34959 who¦34959 love¦34959 me¦34959 and¦34960 who¦34960 obey my instructions¦34961.
\li1
\v 7 You¦34976 mustn't \add ≈wrongly promote\add* the¦34968 name¦34968 of¦34968 Yahweh¦34970 your¦34971 god¦34971, because¦34973 \add *I¦34974\add* won't¦34964 leave¦34975 anyone unpunished¦34975 who¦34978 \add ≈does that\add*.\x + \xo 20:7: \xt Lev 19:12.\x*
\li1
\v 8 \add ≈Keep Saturday different from all the¦34991 other days¦34991\add*\x + \xo 20:8: \xt Exo 16:23-30; 31:12-14.\x*—
\v 9 there's six¦34999 days¦35001 \add every week\add* for working¦35009.\x + \xo 20:9-10: \xt Exo 23:12; 31:15; 34:21; 35:2; Lev 23:3.\x*
\v 10 The¦35013 seventh¦35014 day is¦35016 a rest day for¦35018 Yahweh¦35018 your god¦35019: you¦35023 mustn't do¦35023 any¦35025 work¦35027—not you¦35029, or your children¦35031, or your male¦35035 or female¦35037 servants¦35037, or your cattle, or the¦35013 foreigners¦35041 \add ≈living among you\add*—
\v 11 because¦35049 Yahweh¦35054 made¦35053 the¦35057 heavens¦35057 and¦35058 earth¦35060, the¦35063 sea¦35063, and¦35064 everything that's¦35068 in¦35070 them¦35070 in six¦35050 days¦35052. Then¦35078 he rested¦35071 on¦35070 the seventh¦35073 day, so¦35076 that's why \add *he¦35078\add* blessed¦35077 the rest¦35071 day and¦35083 made it¦35083 sacred¦35083.\x + \xo 20:11: \xt Gen 2:1-3; Exo 31:17.\x*
\li1
\v 12 Honour¦35089 your father¦35089 and¦35090 your mother¦35092, so¦35093 that¦35093 \add ≈you'll have a long¦35094 life\add* on¦35096 the¦35097 land¦35097 that¦35098 your god¦35101 Yahweh¦35100 is¦35102 about¦35102 to¦35102 give¦35102 you.\x + \xo 20:12: a \xt Deu 27:16; Mat 15:4; 19:19; Mrk 7:10; 10:19; Luk 18:20; Eph 6:2; \xo b \xt Eph 6:3.\x*
\li1
