\v 2 If¦35329 you¦35330 buy¦35330 a¦35331 Hebrew¦35332 slave¦35331, he¦35335 should serve¦35335 for six¦35333 years¦35334, then in¦35336 the¦35338 seventh¦35336 year¦35336 he must¦35330 be set free without¦35339 having to¦35338 pay¦35339 you anything.\x + \xo 21:2-6: \xt Lev 25:39-46.\x*
\v 3 If¦35341 he¦35344 came¦35344 by himself, he¦35346 can go¦35346 free by himself. If¦35347 he's¦35351 married with a wife, then his¦35353 wife must¦35344 be¦35349 set free with¦35354 him¦35354.
\v 4 If¦35356 his¦35358 master gave¦35359 him¦35361 a¦35362 wife¦35362 and¦35363 she¦35363 bore¦35363 him¦35365 sons¦35366 or¦35367 daughters¦35368, then the¦35369 wife and¦35370 her children¦35370 are her master's, and only the husband must¦35359 be set free.
\v 5 \add But\add* if¦35377 \add *he¦35380\add* plainly says¦35380, “I love¦35382 my¦35385 master¦35385, my wife¦35388, and¦35389 my children¦35391 so I \add voluntarily\add* choose not¦35392 to be set free¦35394,”
\v 6 then¦35396 his master must take him¦35396 to \add ?≈the place of¦35397 worship¦35415\add*. He¦35411 must bring¦35401 him¦35401 to¦35402 a door¦35404 or¦35405 to¦35406 a doorpost¦35408, and¦35396 his¦35397 master¦35410 must bore a hole his¦35410 ear¦35413 with¦35414 an awl¦35414. Then¦35396 he¦35415 must serve¦35415 him¦35415 \add for life\add*.
\p
\v 7 And¦35423 if a man¦35422 sells¦35421 his¦35425 daughter¦35425 as¦35429 a female¦35426 slave¦35426, she¦35428 \add ≈won't¦35427 be sent away\add* \add after six years\add* like the¦35430 male¦35430 slaves¦35430.
\v 8 If¦35432 the man who¦35437 bought her¦35441 \add ≈wanted her to become his slave-wife\add*, but¦35442 \add later\add* \add ≈he¦35442 isn't¦35445 pleased with¦35449 her behaviour\add*, he must¦35442 allow¦35442 her to be¦35442 bought back by her \add ≈relatives\add*. He¦35447 has¦35449 no authority to sell¦35448 her¦35448 on¦35449 to outsiders, because¦35449 that would \add ≈break the understanding of proper treatment\add* of her¦35451.
\v 9 Or if¦35453 he selected her \add ≈to become his¦35455 son's¦35455 slave-wife\add*, then¦35453 he¦35456 must¦35456 treat her¦35456 \add ≈like a daughter¦35458 would¦35459 expect to¦35461 be treated\add*.
\v 10 If¦35463 he¦35466 \add ≈go on to¦35468 take¦35466 another¦35465 slave-wife\add*, he¦35473 mustn't reduce¦35473 \add @the¦35466 first¦35466 one's¦35466\add* food¦35469 or clothing¦35470, or her¦35469 marital¦35471 rights¦35471,
\v 11 \add but\add* if¦35475 he¦35481 doesn't provide these¦35479 three¦35477 things to¦35482 her¦35482, then¦35475 she¦35483 can go¦35483 free without¦35484 \add ≈having to pay¦35484 anything\add*.
\s1 Rules about violence to others
\rem /s1 The Law concerning Violence; Laws about Violent Acts; Cases of Personal Injury; Personal Injuries
\p
\v 12 Anyone¦35489 who¦35489 strikes¦35489 \add #someone¦35490\add* and¦35491 \add #that¦35489 person\add* dies¦35491, must¦35489 definitely be¦35493 put¦35493 to¦35493 death¦35493.\x + \xo 21:12: \xt Lev 24:17.\x*
\v 13 But¦35495 if \add ≈it wasn't premeditated\add*—if God¦35498 had let¦35499 it happen¦35499 as an accident—then¦35495 I'll¦35501 assign¦35501 a place¦35503 where¦35504 \add @the¦35498 one¦35498 who¦35498 hit¦35498 them¦35498\add* can flee¦35505 to¦35506.\x + \xo 21:13: \xt Num 35:10-34; Deu 19:1-13; Josh 20:1-9.\x*
\v 14 \add However,\add* if \add #someone¦35512\add* \add ≈had schemed to trap and¦35509\add* kill¦35516 \add #their\add* neighbour¦35515, then \add even if the killer clings to\add* my¦35519 altar¦35519, you¦35520 must¦35511 take¦35520 \add #them\add* for execution.
\p
\v 15 Anyone¦35524 who¦35524 strikes¦35524 \add #their\add* father¦35525 or mother¦35526 must¦35524 certainly¦35527 be¦35528 put¦35528 to¦35528 death¦35528.
\p
\v 16 Anyone¦35530 who¦35530 abducts another person—either to sell¦35532 or to keep \add as a slave\add*—\add @that¦35530 person¦35530\add* must¦35530 certainly be¦35533 put¦35536 to¦35536 death¦35536.\x + \xo 21:16: \xt Deu 24:7.\x*
\p
\v 17 Anyone¦35539 who¦35539 curses¦35539 \add #their\add* father¦35540 or mother¦35541 must¦35539 certainly¦35542 be¦35543 put¦35543 to¦35543 death¦35543.\x + \xo 21:17: \xt Lev 20:9; Mat 15:4; Mrk 7:10.\x*
\p
\v 18 If¦35553 \add #two people¦35549\add* fight and¦35550 \add #one\add* hits¦35550 \add #their\add* neighbour¦35555 with¦35556 a stone¦35556 or¦35557 with¦35558 \add #their\add* fist¦35558, and¦35559 \add #the injured one\add* doesn't die¦35560 but¦35546 is bedridden,
\v 19 if¦35564 \add #that person\add* \add eventually\add* rises¦35566 and¦35567 can walk¦35567 about¦35567 outside¦35568 using a staff¦35571, then the \add #person who¦35573 struck¦35573 them\add* is¦35572 free¦35572, other than¦35572 \add ≈reimbursing the costs of¦35575 their lost work and¦35577 their medical expenses\add*.
\p
\v 20 If a \add #master\add* hits¦35583 \add #their\add* male¦35587 or¦35588 female¦35591 slave with¦35592 a staff¦35592 and¦35593 \add @the¦35593 slave¦35593\add* dies¦35593, then the death¦35593 must¦35583 certainly¦35596 be¦35597 avenged¦35596.
\v 21 However¦35608, if¦35600 \add @the slave\add* is able to stand within a¦35602 couple of¦35609 days¦35604, then the \add owner\add* won't¦35606 be¦35607 \add ≈punished\add* because¦35608 \add @the slave\add* is¦35609 \add #their\add* property¦35609.
\p
\v 22 If \add #two people¦35616\add* fight¦35615 together¦35615 and¦35617 strike¦35617 a¦35618 pregnant¦35619 woman and¦35620 \add ≈cause her¦35621 to deliver the baby¦35621\add*, if there's no serious injury¦35624, then he¦35626 must¦35615 certainly¦35625 be¦35626 fined¦35626 whatever the¦35630 husband¦35630 of¦35630 the¦35631 woman¦35631 \add ≈demands\add* and¦35632 the¦35633 judges¦35633 allow.
\v 23 But¦35635 if¦35635 there's serious injury¦35637, then¦35635 you must¦35638 give¦35639 a life¦35640 for a life¦35642,
\v 24 an¦35644 eye¦35644 for an¦35646 eye¦35646, a tooth¦35647 for a tooth¦35649, a hand¦35650 for a hand¦35652, a foot¦35653 for a foot¦35655,\x + \xo 21:24: \xt Lev 24:19-20; Deu 19:21; Mat 5:38.\x*
\v 25 a burn¦35657 for a burn¦35659, a wound for a wound, and a bruise for a bruise.
\p
\v 26 If a \add #master\add* hits¦35670 \add #their\add* male¦35675 or¦35676 female¦35681 slave's¦35675 eye¦35680 and¦35682 damages it¦35682, \add #they\add* must¦35670 let \add @the slave\add* go free¦35684 in¦35685 compensation for the eye¦35686.
\v 27 \add Or\add* if¦35689 the \add #master\add* knocks¦35697 out¦35697 a tooth of¦35695 a male¦35692 or¦35693 female¦35696 slave¦35696, \add #they\add* must¦35697 let \add @the¦35699 slave¦35699\add* go free¦35699 in¦35700 compensation for the tooth¦35701.
\s1 Rules about property
\rem /s1 Laws concerning Property; The Responsibility of Owners
\p
\v 28 If a bull gores¦35706 a man¦35710 or¦35711 a woman¦35714 and¦35715 \add #they\add* die¦35715, the bull must¦35706 certainly¦35716 be¦35717 \add ≈killed¦35717 by throwing rocks¦35716 at it¦35706\add*. The¦35724 owner¦35724 of¦35724 the animal is \add to be considered\add* innocent, \add but\add* its¦35723 meat¦35723 mustn't be eaten¦35720.
\v 29 But¦35728 if¦35728 the bull had¦35734 a habit of¦35735 goring¦35730 in the past and¦35734 its owner was¦35734 warned¦35734 but¦35728 didn't¦35736 keep it¦35737 \add fenced\add* in, and¦35738 it¦35738 kills¦35738 a man¦35739 or¦35740 a woman¦35741, then¦35728 the bull must be¦35729 \add ≈killed¦35738 by throwing rocks¦35743 at¦35735 it\add* and its owner must also¦35734 be put¦35747 to¦35747 death¦35747.
\v 30 If¦35749 a ransom¦35751 payment is¦35752 demanded instead, \add @the¦35756 owner¦35756\add* may buy back \add #their\add* life¦35756 by paying the full amount demanded.
\v 31 Those rules also apply if the¦35771 bull gores a \add person's\add* son¦35765 or¦35767 daughter¦35769.
\v 32 If¦35776 the bull gores¦35779 a male¦35778 or¦35781 female¦35782 slave¦35782, \add @its¦35787 owner¦35787\add* must give¦35787 thirty¦35785 silver¦35783 shekels¦35786 to¦35788 the \add slave owner\add* and¦35789 the¦35789 bull must be¦35790 \add ≈killed¦35790 by throwing rocks¦35790 at it¦35779\add*.
\p
\v 33 If¦35799 \add #someone¦35796\add* uncovers a \add pit for storage\add*, or¦35798 digs¦35801 a \add new one\add* and¦35804 leaves it¦35805 uncovered, and¦35806 a cow¦35809 or¦35810 a donkey¦35811 falls¦35806 into¦35808 it,
\v 34 the¦35813 owner¦35813 of¦35813 the pit¦35814 must pay compensation¦35815. \add @The¦35814 pit¦35814 owner¦35814\add* must pay in cash¦35816, \add but\add* the¦35819 dead¦35819 animal will¦35820 then belong¦35820 to¦35818 them.
\v 35 If \add #one person's bull\add* attacks¦35827 \add someone else's\add* bull and it¦35827 dies¦35835, then they¦35836 should sell¦35836 the live¦35840 animal and¦35841 divide¦35841 the money¦35844 as well as dividing¦35841 up the¦35848 dead¦35848 animal.
\v 36 \add But\add* if¦35853 it was known¦35852 that¦35853 the bull had a habit of¦35861 goring¦35855 in¦35865 the¦35866 past and¦35867 its¦35861 owner¦35861 hadn't kept it \add fenced\add* in, then \add @that¦35863 owner¦35863\add* must¦35863 certainly¦35862 give a live bull for¦35870 the dead one, \add but\add* the dead animal will¦35868 become \add #theirs\add*.
\c 22
\s1 Rules about loss of property or farm animals
\rem /s1 Laws of Restitution; Protection of Property; Laws about Repayment
\p
\v 1 If¦35897 \add #someone\add* steals a cow or a sheep and¦35902 slaughters it or sells it, he¦35900 must¦35900 compensate five cattle for the cow or four sheep for the sheep.
\p
\v 2 (If¦35909 a thief is discovered \add at night\add* while breaking in¦35923, and is struck and dies, \add ≈no one should be¦35922 charged for¦35923 murder\add*.
\v 3 But if¦35926 it's¦35929 daylight already, then that person is¦35929 guilty of¦35930 murder.)
\p \add @A¦35930 thief¦35930\add* who's caught must make¦35941 restitution¦35941, but if \add #they're\add* unable to pay, then \add @the¦35931 thief¦35931\add* must be¦35928 sold \add to cover it\add*.
\v 4 If¦35954 a thief is¦35946 found in¦35959 the¦35959 possession of¦35959 a stolen animal, be¦35946 it¦35958 a cow or a donkey or a sheep, then \add #they\add* must¦35946 pay back another¦35960 matching animal as well.\f + \fr 22:4 \ft Or possibly, must pay back \+bd two\+bd* additional animals.\f*
\p
\v 5 If¦35984 a person releases their livestock to graze \add their own\add* field or¦35977 vineyard, and it¦35973 \add ends up\add* grazing in the someone else's field, \add @the¦35982 owner¦35982 of¦35982 the¦35982 animal¦35982\add* must¦35971 compensate from the best of their field and from the best of their vineyard.
\p
\v 6 If¦35990 a fire breaks out and spreads in \add ≈the bush\add*, and grain that's already stacked or¦35998 is¦36002 still in the¦36003 field gets burnt up, the¦36004 person¦36004 who started the fire must¦35992 certainly pay¦35992 compensation.
\p
\v 7 If¦36024 \add #anyone\add* gives their neighbour¦36031 money or goods for safekeeping, and¦36018 if¦36025 it is stolen from the¦36030 neighbour's¦36031 house¦36021, if the thief¦36017 is found¦36016, \add #they\add* must¦36016 pay double in¦36030 compensation.
\v 8 If¦36060 the¦36065 thief can't be found, then the¦36067 owner of¦36067 the house must¦36059 be¦36062 brought to¦36064 \add ?≈the judges¦36072 for God's¦36065 decision\add* as¦36071 to whether or not \add #they¦36071\add* have \add ≈improperly handled\add* \add #their¦36069\add* neighbour's¦36075 property.
\p
\v 9 Concerning every other squabble about any cattle or a donkey¦36086 or sheep¦36092, or¦36098 about clothing or¦36101 any lost property that's¦36105 under dispute, both parties must go to \add ?≈the judges for God's decision\add*—anyone¦36082 who¦36105 God declares to be guilty must pay¦36081 his¦36085 neighbour¦36085 double as compensation.
\p
\v 10 If¦36109 anyone gives \add #their¦36112\add* neighbour¦36119 a donkey or a cow or a sheep or any animal to look after, and¦36120 it¦36120 dies or is¦36110 injured or disappears without anyone seeing,
\v 11 both of them must declare in front of Yahweh as to¦36132 whether or not they \add ≈improperly handled\add* \add #their\add* neighbour's property. The owner¦36132 must accept \add <the sworn statement\add* and¦36126 no compensation is¦36129 required,
\v 12 \add but\add* if¦36135 it¦36138 was¦36138 truly stolen from \add @the¦36139 neighbour¦36139\add*, \add #they\add* must¦36138 pay compensation to the¦36141 owner.
\v 13 If it¦36153 was¦36153 truly \add ≈killed by a some other animal\add*, \add @the¦36152 neighbour¦36152\add* must¦36149 bring \add @the¦36149 remains¦36149\add* as evidence, and¦36147 no compensation is¦36153 required.
\p
\v 14 If¦36165 anyone borrows \add <an animal¦36173\add* from \add #their\add* neighbour and it gets injured or dies without the owner¦36167 being¦36173 with¦36176 it, \add @the¦36170 person¦36170 who¦36170 borrowed¦36170 it¦36170\add* must¦36170 pay compensation,
\v 15 \add but\add* if its owner was¦36188 \add there\add* with¦36190 it¦36190, no compensation is required—if it¦36193 was for¦36194 hire, then that was included in its hiring fee.
\s1 More rules about everyday life
\rem /s1 Social and Religious Laws; Moral and Religious Laws; Social Responsibility
\p
\v 16 If¦36197 a man entices a young woman who's not engaged, and sleeps with her, he¦36200 must¦36200 certainly pay¦36202 the¦36206 bride¦36206 price¦36204 \add to her father\add* for her to¦36206 become his wife.\x + \xo 22:16-17: \xt Deu 22:28-29.\x*
\v 17 If her father absolutely refuses to give her to him, \add @the¦36213 man¦36213\add* must¦36213 \add still\add* pay the normal bride price in cash.
\p
\v 18 You must¦36224 execute any¦36217 woman who¦36219 practices sorcery.\x + \xo 22:18: \xt Deu 18:10-11.\x*
\p
\v 19 Anyone¦36232 who¦36228 has sex with an animal must¦36230 be¦36230 executed.\x + \xo 22:19: \xt Lev 18:23; 20:15-16; Deu 27:21.\x*
\p
\v 20 You¦36239 must¦36239 execute anyone who offers a sacrifice to any god other than Yahweh¦36247.\x + \xo 22:20: \xt Deu 17:2-7.\x*
\p
\v 21 You mustn't disadvantage or oppress¦36255 any¦36250 \add ≈foreigner staying in your country\add*, because you were \add ≈foreigners staying\add* in the land of¦36250 Egypt.\x + \xo 22:21-22: \xt Exo 23:9; Lev 19:33-34; Deu 24:17-18; 27:19.\x*
\v 22 You¦36270 mustn't mistreat any widow or any fatherless child,
\v 23 \add because\add* if you¦36277 \add *do¦36278\add* and¦36274 they¦36279 ask me to help them, I'll¦36277 help them
\v 24 and get angry. I'll cause you¦36291 all to¦36291 die in battle, and your wives will become widows and your \add #children\add* will become fatherless.
\p
\v 25 If¦36311 you¦36314 loan money to any my people who are poor, you¦36321 mustn't act like an \add impartial\add* creditor to¦36322 \add #them\add*—you mustn't charge \add #them\add* interest.\x + \xo 22:25: \xt Lev 25:35-38; Deu 15:7-11; 23:19-20.\x*
\v 26 If¦36344 you actually take the your neighbour's \add ≈cloak¦36331\add* as a security, you must¦36334 return it¦36326 to¦36339 \add #them\add* by sunset,\x + \xo 22:26-27: \xt Deu 24:10-13.\x*
\v 27 because it's \add #their\add* only covering. What else could \add #they\add* cover themselves with¦36352 when \add #they\add* try to sleep? If \add #they\add* cry out to me, I'll \add ≈act on¦36352 it\add*, because I'm compassionate.
\p
\v 28 You¦36360 mustn't insult God, and¦36358 don't¦36359 curse your¦36362 leaders.\x + \xo 22:28: \xt Acts 23:5.\x*
\p
\v 29 You¦36370 mustn't \add fail to give\add* me¦36383 the best parts of¦36371 the grain that you harvest, or \add the best\add* olive oil or wine that you produce.
\p You must¦36370 give¦36381 your¦36371 firstborn sons to me,
\v 30 plus¦36386 you must do the same with your cattle and your sheep and goats. The¦36398 young must stay seven days with \add #their\add* mothers, then you must give \add #them\add* to¦36396 me¦36390 on the¦36392 eighth day.
\p
\v 31 You must be \add ≈different from others because you're dedicated to me\add*. \add So\add* you mustn't eat the meat of animals that are mauled in the countryside—throw it to the dogs \add instead\add*.\x + \xo 22:31: \xt Lev 17:15.\x*
\c 23
\s1 Rules about honesty and kindness
\rem /s1 Justice for All; Justice and Fairness; Laws of Justice and Mercy; A Call for Justice
\p
\v 1 You¦36402 mustn't present a false statement. Don't¦36401 conspire with¦36409 a wicked¦36411 \add >person¦36411\add* to¦36412 give false evidence.\x + \xo 23:1: \xt Exo 20:16; Lev 19:11-12; Deu 5:20.\x*
\v 2 Don't¦36417 \add just\add* follow the crowd into¦36423 doing what's wrong¦36423, and¦36424 don't¦36417 \add just\add* say what others say in court \add if it's untrue\add*,
\v 3 and¦36435 don't¦36436 \add automatically\add* favour the poor¦36435 in¦36438 court either.\x + \xo 23:3: \xt Lev 19:15.\x*
\p
\v 4 If¦36441 you¦36442 come across your¦36444 enemy's¦36444 cow¦36443 or¦36445 donkey¦36446 going astray, you must¦36442 certainly¦36448 take¦36449 it¦36449 back to¦36450 \add #them\add*.\x + \xo 23:4-5: \xt Deu 22:1-4.\x*
\v 5 If¦36453 you¦36455 see¦36455 that the¦36456 donkey¦36456 of¦36456 someone¦36457 who¦36457 hates¦36457 you has fallen to¦36463 the ground under¦36459 its¦36460 load¦36460, you mustn't \add ≈just walk way\add*—you must¦36455 certainly¦36464 help \add #them\add* \add ≈with¦36466 it¦36466\add*.
\p
\v 6 You¦36470 mustn't deny justice¦36471 to the¦36471 poor in¦36473 \add #their\add* lawsuits¦36473.\x + \xo 23:6-8: \xt Lev 19:15; Deu 16:19.\x*
\v 7 Stay far way from¦36475 deceptive words¦36475. You¦36478 mustn't kill¦36483 innocent or honest \add >people\add* because¦36484 I¦36487 won't¦36481 \add allow\add* wicked¦36488 \add >people¦36488\add* to be¦36478 declared¦36487 innocent.
\v 8 You¦36493 mustn't accept¦36492 \add #bribes\add*, because¦36493 \add #bribes¦36494\add* \add ≈stop people from being unbiased\add* and¦36497 \add #they\add* undermine the¦36498 words¦36498 of¦36498 \add ≈honest\add* \add >people\add*.
\p
\v 9 You¦36506 mustn't oppress¦36503 \add #foreigners\add* since you \add #yourselves\add* know¦36505 \add ≈how that feels\add* because¦36510 you all were¦36513 foreigners in¦36514 Egypt¦36515.\x + \xo 23:9: \xt Exo 22:21; Lev 19:33-34; Deu 24:17-18; 27:19.\x*
\s1 The seventh year and the seventh day
\rem /s1 Sabbath Laws; Sabbatical Year and Sabbath; The Seventh Year and the Seventh Day
\p
\v 10 You¦36519 should plant your¦36522 land¦36522 and¦36517 gather¦36523 its¦36526 produce¦36526 for six¦36517 years¦36518,\x + \xo 23:10-11: \xt Lev 25:1-7.\x*
\v 11 \add but\add* in the¦36528 seventh¦36528 \add >year¦36528\add* you¦36529 must let¦36529 \add @the¦36531 harvest¦36531\add* drop and¦36534 \add just\add* leave¦36534 it there and \add allow\add* the poor people¦36533 to eat it. Then¦36528 the animals¦36536 in the¦36537 countryside¦36537 can eat the reminder. You¦36540 must \add also\add* do¦36540 that to¦36541 your vineyards¦36541 and your olive¦36542 orchards¦36542.
\p
\v 12 Six¦36544 days¦36545 You¦36546 should¦36552 work¦36547 for six¦36544 days, then on¦36548 the¦36549 seventh¦36549 \add >day¦36548\add* you¦36550 must¦36546 rest¦36550 so¦36551 that¦36551 your cow¦36553 and your donkey¦36554 can rest, and¦36555 the¦36556 \add #children¦36556\add* of¦36556 your¦36558 \add #slaves¦36558\add* and the foreigner \add staying in your land\add* can be refreshed¦36555.\x + \xo 23:12: \xt Exo 20:9-11; 31:15; 34:21; 35:2; Lev 23:3; Deu 5:13-14.\x*
\p
\v 13 \add ≈Take¦36566 careful notice of¦36567\add* everything that¦36562 I've¦36564 told¦36564 you all. You all mustn't \add invoke\add* other¦36569 gods¦36568—\add in fact\add* \add ≈don't¦36570 even mention their names¦36567\add*.
\s1 Three compulsory celebrations each year
\rem /s1 Three Annual Festivals; The Annual Festivals; The Three Great Festivals; The Three Annual Festivals
\r (Exo. 34:18-26; Deu. 16:1-17)
\p
\v 14 You¦36580 must¦36580 celebrate¦36580 me¦36581 three¦36578 times every year¦36582.
\v 15 \add 1/\add* You¦36588 must observe¦36588 the¦36586 \it Flat¦36587 Bread¦36587 Celebration\it*. You¦36591 must eat¦36591 unleavened¦36592 bread¦36587 for seven¦36589 days¦36590 as¦36593 I¦36594 commanded¦36594 you¦36594, in¦36600 late March or early April because¦36598 that's when you¦36601 came¦36601 out¦36601 from¦36602 Egypt¦36602. You mustn't come¦36601 without an offering¦36605.\x + \xo 23:15: \xt Exo 12:14-20; Lev 23:6-8; Num 28:17-25.\x*
\p
\v 16 \add 2/\add* You¦36614 must observe the \it \+add Spring\+add* Harvest¦36610 Celebration\it*, bringing the¦36611 first¦36611 portion of¦36616 your¦36612 harvests¦36610 from¦36624 what you¦36620 planted.
\p \add 3/\add* You must observe the \it \+add Finished\+add* Harvest Celebration\it* at¦36618 the end¦36618 of the¦36619 year¦36619, after you've¦36620 finished harvesting \add ≈everything you planted\add*.
\v 17 \add So\add* all¦36632 your¦36634 males¦36634 must¦36631 gather in¦36630 front of¦36632 the¦36637 master¦36638 Yahweh¦36640 three¦36628 times¦36629 each year¦36630.
\p
\v 18 You¦36644 mustn't sacrifice¦36644 the¦36648 blood¦36648 of¦36648 my¦36650 sacrifices¦36650 together with¦36645 bread \add ≈that's been risen\add*, and¦36651 all the¦36654 fat¦36654 \add must be burnt during the night\add* so that none remains¦36653 in the morning¦36659.
\p
\v 19 You¦36664 must¦36664 bring¦36664 the \add ≈best\add* of the firstfruits¦36661 of your¦36663 \add ≈harvests\add* to the¦36665 house¦36665 of¦36665 Yahweh¦36666 your god¦36667.
\rem /s1 The Conquest of Canaan Promised; A Promise of the Lord's Presence; Promises and Instructions; God's Angel to Prepare the Way
\p You¦36670 mustn't boil¦36670 a¦36671 young goat in¦36672 its¦36673 mother's¦36673 milk¦36672.\x + \xo 23:19: \xt Deu 26:2; Exo 34:26; Deu 14:21.\x*
\s1 Promises and teachings
\p
\v 20 Listen, I'm¦36677 about¦36678 to¦36678 send¦36678 a messenger¦36679 \add ≈in¦36682 front¦36680 of you\add* to¦36681 guard¦36681 you¦36681 on¦36682 the way¦36682, and¦36683 to¦36683 take¦36683 you¦36683 to¦36684 the¦36686 place¦36686 that¦36687 I¦36688 have¦36688 prepared¦36688.
\v 21 \add ≈Stay behind him¦36691\add* and¦36692 listen¦36692 to¦36693 \add ≈what he says\add*. Don't¦36694 \add ≈annoy\add* him because he won't¦36694 \add ≈put up with¦36693 disobedience\add* because¦36698 \add ≈he¦36700 represents my¦36703 authority\add*.
\v 22 \add But\add* if¦36707 you \add ≈take careful¦36709 notice of¦36711 his¦36711 words\add* and¦36712 do¦36712 everything that¦36714 I¦36715 say¦36715, then I'll be¦36716 an¦36716 enemy¦36716 to¦36716 your¦36719 enemies¦36719 and¦36720 I'll be against those who are against you.
\v 23 My¦36728 messenger¦36728 will¦36727 go¦36727 \add ≈ahead of¦36728 you\add* and¦36730 take¦36730 you¦36730 to¦36731 \add face\add* the¦36733 Amorites¦36733, the¦36734 Hittites¦36734, the¦36735 Perizzites¦36735, the¦36736 Canaanites¦36736, the¦36737 Hivites¦36737, and¦36738 the¦36738 Yebusites¦36738, and¦36739 then I'll¦36739 annihilate¦36739 them.
\v 24 You¦36750 mustn't serve¦36746 or bow¦36743 down¦36743 to¦36744 their gods¦36744, and¦36745 you¦36746 mustn't do \add @what¦36746 those¦36746 people¦36746\add* do, because¦36750 you¦36752 must¦36752 completely overthrow them¦36752 and¦36753 completely smash their \add sacred\add* stone pillars¦36755.
\v 25 You all must¦36757 worship¦36757 your god¦36760 Yahweh¦36759, and¦36761 he'll¦36761 bless¦36761 your food¦36764 and your water¦36767. I'll¦36768 keep sickness¦36769 away from¦36770 you¦36770
\v 26 \add and\add* there won't be¦36773 \add #any miscarriages¦36774\add* or \add #women\add* in¦36776 your land¦36776 that can't conceive. I'll¦36781 ensure \add ≈that you live your full\add* number¦36779 of¦36776 days¦36780.
\p
\v 27 I'll \add ≈go¦36795 ahead of you and¦36797 will¦36797 terrify¦36785\add* and¦36788 confuse¦36788 all¦36800 of the¦36793 people¦36793 \add groups\add* \add ≈whose lands you'll¦36795 enter\add*, and I'll \add ≈cause them¦36796 to¦36803 flee from you in¦36796 battle\add*.
\v 28 I'll¦36806 send¦36806 hornets¦36809 \add ≈ahead¦36821 of¦36821 you\add* and \add #they'll\add* drive¦36811 out¦36811 the¦36814 Hivites¦36814, the¦36817 Canaanites¦36817, and¦36818 the¦36820 Hittites¦36820 \add ≈before¦36821 you¦36821 get there\add*.
\v 29 I¦36824 won't drive¦36824 them out¦36824 \add ≈more than¦36825 a year¦36826 ahead¦36825 of¦36825 you¦36825\add* in¦36826 case the area becomes¦36830 desolate¦36832 and¦36833 the¦36835 \add ≈wild animals¦36835 proliferate too much\add* in the¦36836 countryside¦36836.
\v 30 I'll¦36846 drive¦36840 them out¦36840 little by little \add ≈ahead¦36841 of¦36841 you¦36841\add* until¦36842 \add ≈your¦36841 numbers increase\add* and¦36845 you¦36845 take¦36845 over the¦36848 land¦36848.
\v 31 Then¦36850 I'll \add ≈help you¦36872 establish\add* your¦36873 borders¦36853 from¦36854 the¦36854 Red Sea¦36854 to¦36857 the Mediterranean, and¦36861 from¦36861 the¦36861 wilderness¦36861 to¦36862 the¦36864 \add Euphrates\add* river¦36864, because¦36865 I'll \add ≈help you defeat the¦36870 existing\add* inhabitants¦36870 of¦36870 the¦36871 land¦36871 and¦36872 so you'll¦36872 drive¦36872 them¦36872 right out¦36872.
\v 32 You¦36877 mustn't make¦36877 any agreement¦36880 with \add @those¦36878 people¦36878\add* or with their¦36879 gods¦36879.
\v 33 They¦36883 mustn't live¦36883 in¦36884 your¦36884 land¦36884, in case¦36887 they¦36887 cause¦36887 you¦36888 to¦36889 sin¦36887 against me¦36889. Their¦36894 gods¦36894 would¦36897 certainly become¦36897 a trap¦36899 for¦36898 you, and then you'd \add end up\add* worshipping them.
\c 24
\s1 The people confirm their agreement
\rem /s1 Israel Accepts the Lord's Covenant; The Covenant Is Sealed; The Blood of the Covenant; The Covenant Confirmed
\p
\v 1 Then \add @Yahweh¦36909\add* told¦36905 Mosheh¦36904, “Come¦36906 up¦36906 \add the mountain\add* to¦36907 \add *me¦36909\add*—you¦36910, Aharon¦36911, Nadab¦36912, Abihu¦36913 and¦36914 seventy¦36914 of¦36916 the Israeli¦36916 elders¦36915, and¦36917 you must¦36917 \add stay\add* at a distance¦36918 to worship¦36917.
\v 2 Then¦36925 Mosheh¦36921 alone¦36922 must¦36920 approach¦36931 \add *me\add*, \add but\add* \add @the¦36926 others¦36926\add* mustn't come near¦36920, and¦36920 \add also\add* the¦36929 people¦36929 mustn't come¦36931 up¦36931 with¦36932 him¦36932.”
\p
\v 3 \add So\add* Mosheh¦36935 went¦36934 and¦36934 explained to¦36937 the people¦36950 \add ≈everything that Yahweh had¦36959 said¦36953, including¦36936\add* all the regulations. Then¦36934 all of¦36944 the¦36946 people answered¦36947 \add ≈in unison\add*, “We'll do everything that Yahweh has¦36959 \add ≈told¦36953 us to do¦36961\add*.”
\v 4 \add So\add* Mosheh¦36964 wrote¦36963 \add ≈down everything that Yahweh¦36969 had instructed\add*. Then¦36963 he¦36963 got up early¦36970 in¦36971 the morning¦36971 and¦36972 built¦36972 an¦36973 altar¦36973 at¦36971 the bottom of the mountain¦36975 and¦36976 \add set up\add* twelve stone pillars¦36978 for¦36979 the¦36981 twelve tribes¦36981 of¦36981 Yisrael¦36982,
\v 5 and¦36984 he¦36984 sent¦36984 some young¦36987 men¦36987 to offer¦36990 burnt¦36991 offerings¦36991 and¦36992 to sacrifice¦36992 some bulls¦36996 as peace¦36994 offerings¦36994 to¦36995 Yahweh¦36995.
\v 6 Mosheh¦36999 took¦36998 half of the blood \add from the sacrifices\add* and¦36998 put¦37002 it¦37002 into¦37003 basins¦37003. He¦36998 sprinkled¦37006 \add the other\add* half of the blood onto the altar¦37009.
\v 7 Then¦37011 he¦37011 took¦37011 the scroll with¦37015 the agreement¦37013 \add written on it\add* and¦37014 read it¦37014 out loud to the people¦37016, and¦37017 they¦37017 \add ≈responded¦37017\add*, “We'll obey¦37024 everything that¦37019 Yahweh¦37022 has¦37021 instructed.”
\p
\v 8 Then¦37026 Mosheh¦37027 took¦37026 the blood \add in the bowls\add* and¦37026 sprinkled¦37031 it¦37035 onto the people¦37034, telling¦37035 \add <them\add*, “Look. \add This is\add* the¦37037 blood¦37037 \add confirming\add* the¦37039 agreement¦37039 that¦37040 Yahweh¦37042 has¦37041 made¦37041 with¦37043 you according to \add ≈what you just heard\add*.”\x + \xo 24:8: a \xt Mat 26:28; Mrk 14:24; Luk 22:20; 1Cor 11:25; Heb 10:29; \xo b \xt Heb 9:19-20.\x*
\rem /s1 On the Mountain with God
\p
\v 9 Then¦37050 Mosheh¦37051, Aharon¦37052, Nadab¦37053, Abihu¦37054, and¦37050 seventy¦37055 Israeli¦37057 elders¦37056 climbed up \add the mountain\add*
\v 10 and¦37059 they¦37059 saw¦37059 the¦37061 god¦37061 of¦37061 Yisrael¦37062. Under¦37060 his¦37064 feet¦37064 was something like¦37065 a tile made¦37065 of sapphire¦37067 that \add ≈looked¦37059 so pure that it was¦37063 as¦37068 clear¦37070\add* as the sky¦37069.
\v 11 Those¦37076 Israeli¦37075 leaders saw¦37080 God¦37083 and \add ≈yet they weren't harmed by him.\add*. Then¦37072 they ate¦37084 and¦37085 drank¦37085 \add together\add*.
\s1 Mosheh's long stay on Mt. Sinai
\rem /s1 Moses on Mount Sinai
\p
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦37089 told¦37088 Mosheh¦37092, “Come¦37093 up¦37093 to¦37094 me¦37094 on the¦37095 mountain¦37095 and¦37096 \add wait\add* there¦37098, and I will give¦37099 you some stone¦37104 slabs with the¦37105 rules and¦37106 regulations that¦37107 I have¦37108 written¦37108 \add on them so you can\add* to¦37109 teach¦37109 them¦37109 \add <to the people\add*.”
\v 13 \add So\add* Mosheh¦37112 and¦37113 his¦37114 assistant¦37114 Yehoshua¦37113 set off, and Mosheh climbed up¦37111 God's mountain¦37119.
\v 14 He¦37125 had \add already\add* told¦37125 the¦37124 elders¦37124, “Wait for¦37128 us¦37128 \add down here\add* in¦37129 this¦37129 place¦37129 until¦37130 we¦37133 return¦37133 \add here\add* to¦37134 you all. And¦37135 see¦37135, Aharon¦37136 and¦37122 Hur¦37137 are¦37138 with¦37129 you—\add ≈any leader judging matters¦37142 requiring more wisdom can approach¦37143\add* them¦37144 \add for help\add*.”
\p
\v 15 Then¦37153 Mosheh¦37147 went to¦37148 \add the base of\add* the mountain¦37155 and¦37151 a cloud¦37152 covered¦37151 \add over\add* \add *it¦37146\add*.
\v 16 Yahweh's¦37160 \add ≈radiance\add* settled¦37157 on Mt¦37163. Sinai¦37164, and¦37157 the cloud covered¦37165 it¦37157 for six¦37167 days¦37168, then¦37157 on the seventh¦37174 day¦37173 he¦37169 called¦37169 to¦37170 Mosheh¦37172 from¦37175 within the cloud¦37176.
\v 17 The¦37179 appearance¦37178 of Yahweh's¦37180 \add ≈radiance\add* was¦37181 like¦37181 a \add ≈roaring\add* fire¦37181 on¦37183 the¦37183 top¦37183 of¦37183 the¦37184 mountain¦37184 \add ≈from what the Israelis¦37187 below could see\add*.
\v 18 Then¦37189 Mosheh¦37190 entered \add into\add* the cloud¦37192 and¦37193 continued up the¦37196 mountain¦37196, and¦37197 \add *he¦37197\add* remained up there for forty¦37200 full days¦37201.\x + \xo 24:18: \xt Deu 9:9.\x*
\c 25
\s1 Contributions for God's tent
\rem /s1 Offerings for the Sacred Tent; Offerings for the Tabernacle
\r (Exo. 35:4-9)
\p
\v 1 Yahweh¦37207 told¦37211 Mosheh¦37210,
\v 2 “Tell the¦37216 Israelis¦37217 that they¦37218 should \add ≈raise funds\add* for me¦37220. You should collect a contribution¦37221 from¦37222 every¦37223 \add #family\add* that's¦37218 willing to¦37220 donate.
\v 3 You should accept¦37237 contributions¦37235 of gold¦37239, silver¦37240, or bronze¦37241,
\v 4 as well as yarn \add dyed\add* blue, purple¦37244, or crimson¦37245, plus¦37244 finely-spun linen¦37247 and¦37243 \add spun\add* goat¦37248 hair¦37248,
\v 5 and¦37250 red-dyed ram¦37251 skins¦37250, fine leather¦37253, and¦37255 acacia¦37256 timber¦37255.
\v 6 \add Also\add* lamp oil¦37258, spices¦37260 for¦37259 \add making\add* anointing¦37262 oil and¦37263 fragrant¦37264 incense¦37263,
\v 7 onyx¦37268 and¦37269 \add other\add* gemstones for¦37271 setting¦37270 into the apron¦37271 and¦37272 the breastplate¦37272.
\v 8 Then¦37274 they¦37274 should make¦37274 me¦37275 a¦37276 residence \add so\add* I¦37277 can live¦37277 \add in it\add* among¦37278 them¦37278,
\v 9 according¦37280 to the¦37286 \add #patterns¦37286\add* that¦37281 I'll¦37282 show¦37283 you¦37284 for the¦37287 residence¦37287 and¦37288 for all of its¦37292 utensils¦37292. You¦37284 all must¦37294 make¦37294 \add ≈all of it exactly to plan\add*.
\s1 The box to hold the stone slabs
\rem /s1 Plans for the Ark; The Ark of the Covenant; The Covenant Box; The Ark
\r (Exo. 37:1-9)
\p
\v 10 They¦37297 must¦37297 make¦37297 a wooden¦37299 chest¦37298 from acacia¦37300 wood¦37299. It should be¦37301 125cm long¦37303, with the width¦37306 and¦37302 the height¦37309 being 75cm.
\v 11 It¦37312 must¦37311 be overlaid¦37311 with pure¦37314 gold \add sheeting\add* on¦37319 the outside¦37316 and the inside¦37315, and have a gold moulding¦37320 \add fitted\add* all¦37322 around¦37322 it¦37312.
\v 12 Four¦37326 gold¦37328 rings must¦37324 be¦37335 cast¦37324 and¦37324 attached to the¦37338 four¦37331 feet¦37332—two rings on¦37341 each side¦37343.
\v 13 Make¦37351 two \add carrying\add* poles¦37347 from acacia¦37349 wood¦37348 and¦37350 overlay¦37350 them¦37351 with gold¦37352 \add sheeting\add*.
\v 14 Those poles¦37357 will¦37354 be inserted through¦37366 the rings¦37358 on¦37359 the¦37360 sides¦37360 of¦37360 the¦37361 chest¦37361 so it can be \add picked up and\add* carried¦37362 on them¦37366.
\v 15 The¦37368 poles¦37371 must¦37370 be kept in¦37368 the rings¦37368 on the¦37369 chest¦37369—they mustn't be removed¦37373.
\v 16 The¦37379 \add ≈two stone slabs that¦37382 I'll¦37383 give¦37383 you¦37384 with our agreement inscribed on them\add* must¦37376 be placed¦37376 inside the¦37381 chest¦37379.
\p
\v 17 You¦37386 must make¦37386 a¦37391 lid the same length¦37392 and width¦37395 as the chest. It must be made¦37386 of¦37392 pure¦37389 gold¦37388 \add and will be known as\add* ‘the atonement¦37387 platform’.\x + \xo 25:17: \xt Heb 9:5.\x*
\v 18 Then¦37403 make¦37397 a pair of winged-creatures from gold¦37400 that's hammered¦37401 from¦37404 the¦37404 two¦37404 ends¦37405 of¦37405 the¦37406 atonement¦37406 platform.
\v 19 \add Yes,\add* make¦37408 one¦37410 winged-creature from¦37411 each end¦37411 of¦37427 the¦37420 gold lid material.
\v 20 \add *Their¦37436\add* up-lifted wings¦37433 should spread¦37432 out¦37432 covering¦37435 the¦37439 atonement¦37439 platform and¦37430 they¦37448 should be¦37448 facing each¦37441 other across the top of¦37449 the¦37450 platform.
\v 21 When¦37452 I¦37468 give¦37468 you¦37452 the stone slabs, put¦37452 them inside the¦37458 box¦37458 and¦37452 then¦37452 fasten the¦37455 atonement¦37455 platform on¦37456 top to¦37469 form the lid.
\v 22 Then¦37471 I'll meet¦37471 with¦37475 you there¦37473, and¦37474 from¦37476 the¦37477 atonement¦37477 platform between¦37478 the¦37479 two¦37479 winged-creatures and above¦37482 the stone slabs, I'll be¦37482 able to tell¦37474 you¦37475 my commands¦37490 to pass on to the¦37494 Israelis¦37495.
\s1 The bread offering table
\rem /s1 The Table for the Bread of the Presence; Plans for the Table; The Table for the Bread Offered to God; The Table
\r (Exo. 37:10-16)
\p
\v 23 You¦37498 must¦37498 make¦37498 a table¦37499 from acacia¦37501 wood¦37500: one metre long¦37503, 500cm wide¦37505, and¦37498 750cm high¦37508.
\v 24 Overlay¦37511 it with pure¦37513 gold and¦37510 have a gold¦37512 moulding¦37516 fitted all¦37518 around¦37518 it.
\v 25 Make¦37520 an 8cm wide¦37523 rim around¦37524 it¦37521 and¦37520 fit a¦37522 gold¦37528 moulding¦37526 onto the rim¦37529.
\v 26 Make¦37538 four gold¦37536 rings¦37535 and¦37532 attach them near the¦37540 legs on¦37541 the¦37542 four¦37542 corners¦37543 \add of the table\add*
\v 27 near the¦37549 rim¦37549. \add @The¦37551 rings¦37551\add* are¦37550 so poles¦37553 can be¦37550 inserted in order to¦37552 carry¦37554 the¦37557 table¦37557.
\v 28 Make¦37559 \add two\add* poles¦37562 out of¦37563 acacia¦37564 wood¦37563 and¦37559 overlaid¦37565 them¦37566 with¦37570 gold¦37567 for carrying¦37568 the¦37573 table¦37573.
\v 29 \add In addition,\add* make¦37575 the necessary plates¦37576 and¦37577 pans¦37577, and¦37578 the pitchers¦37578 and¦37579 bowls¦37579 to be¦37581 used for pouring¦37581 out¦37581 \add <the wine offerings\add*—all from pure¦37584 gold¦37583.
\v 30 You¦37588 must¦37588 keep sacred bread¦37592 on¦37589 the¦37591 table¦37591 continually¦37595 in front¦37594 of¦37592 me.\x + \xo 25:30: \xt Lev 24:5-8.\x*
\s1 The lampstand
\rem /s1 The Lampstand; Plans for the Lampstand
\r (Exo. 37:17-24)
\p
\v 31 You¦37598 must¦37598 make¦37598 a lampstand¦37599 from¦37610 pure¦37601 gold¦37600. The¦37604 base¦37605 and¦37606 shaft¦37606 are to be¦37603 hammered¦37602 out \add of one piece of gold\add* as well as its¦37606 cups¦37607 and \add decorative\add* buds and flowers¦37609.
\v 32 There must¦37615 be¦37615 six¦37613 branches¦37614 extending from¦37616 the¦37622 shaft—three¦37623 on each side¦37626.
\v 33 Three¦37629 cups¦37630 shaped¦37631 like¦37631 almond¦37631 flowers must¦37632 be on¦37632 each branch¦37645 along with¦37632 a bud and¦37635 petals.
\v 34 The¦37651 \add centre\add* shaft must¦37651 have four¦37652 cups¦37653 like¦37654 almond¦37654 flowers along with¦37651 a bud and¦37651 petals¦37656.
\v 35 For¦37674 each of the three pairs of branches \add (one branch out each side in each pair)\add*, make a bud \add on the centre shaft\add* so each pair of branches appear to be¦37659 growing out of¦37660 it¦37662.
\v 36 These buds and¦37682 their¦37681 branches¦37682 must¦37684 all¦37685 be¦37686 hammered¦37686 out from¦37683 \add that\add* single¦37687 piece of¦37681 pure¦37689 gold¦37688.
\v 37 Make¦37691 seven¦37695 lamps¦37694 and¦37691 set them up¦37696 on¦37701 it to give¦37700 light¦37700 out from the¦37703 front¦37704 of¦37699 it¦37700,
\v 38 and¦37706 make all the utensils and¦37707 dishes for the lamps from pure¦37709 gold¦37708.
\v 39 This can all¦37717 be made¦37714 from 35kg of¦37717 pure¦37713 gold¦37712
\v 40 and¦37723 be sure to make¦37723 it all like the pattern¦37724 that¦37725 you're¦37727 being¦37728 shown¦37728 on¦37724 the mountain¦37729.\x + \xo 25:40: \xt Acts 7:44; Heb 8:5.\x*
\c 26
\s1 Plans for the sacred residence
\rem /s1 Plans for the Tabernacle; The Tabernacle; The Tent of the Lord's Presence
\r (Exo. 36:8-38)
\p
\v 1 You¦37735 must make¦37735 \add &my\add* residence with ten¦37736 fabric panels formed by a skilled¦37746 craftsman. They must be made¦37745 from twisted¦37739 finely-spun linen¦37738, with winged-creatures \add embroidered on them using\add* blue, purple¦37741, and¦37742 scarlet¦37743 thread.
\v 2 The¦37752 hanging panels must¦37754 all¦37764 be¦37754 the¦37757 same size¦37762: 14.5m long¦37750 and¦37755 two metres¦37756 wide¦37757.
\v 3 Five¦37776 of¦37769 the¦37769 panels will¦37770 be¦37770 coupled together \add as one set\add* and¦37776 the other five¦37776 as another.
\v 4 For each set¦37792, make¦37784 loops¦37785 of blue cloth and¦37793 fasten them along the outer¦37797 edge¦37795 of each of the end¦37791 panels—
\v 5 place fifty¦37806 loops on¦37804 the end¦37809 of¦37809 each set¦37812 so that¦37811 the¦37813 loops are¦37814 opposite¦37814 each¦37816 other.
\v 6 You'll¦37827 also¦37825 need to make fifty¦37822 gold¦37824 clips to join¦37825 the¦37836 two sets together to make a single¦37837 walled structure.
\p
\v 7 You¦37852 must¦37840 make¦37840 eleven panels with goats' hair¦37842 to¦37843 form a¦37843 tent¦37846 over¦37844 the¦37846 residence¦37846.
\v 8 Each of¦37854 the eleven panels must¦37858 be¦37858 the same size¦37865: 15m long¦37854 and¦37860 two metres¦37859 wide¦37860.
\v 9 You¦37871 must¦37871 join¦37871 five¦37874 panels into a set, and¦37871 six¦37879 panels into the other set so that the sixth¦37886 panel can be doubled¦37882 over at the front¦37889 of¦37891 the¦37891 tent¦37891.
\v 10 You¦37893 must¦37893 make¦37893 50 loops¦37895 to go onto the¦37897 end of¦37897 one¦37899 set¦37901, and¦37902 another 50 for the¦37905 edge¦37905 of¦37905 the other set¦37907.
\v 11 You'll also¦37914 need to make fifty¦37913 bronze¦37912 clips to join¦37919 the two sets together¦37919 to make the¦37922 tent¦37922 cover.
\v 12 Let the extra half¦37930 panel hang over¦37934 the¦37935 back of¦37936 the¦37936 residence¦37936.
\v 13 The¦37938 half metre of¦37943 extra length¦37943 on¦37942 each side¦37950 that¦37939 extends beyond the linen sets will¦37946 hang \add evenly\add* over¦37948 the¦37950 sides¦37950.
\p
\v 14 You¦37956 must¦37956 make¦37956 a covering of¦37959 rams¦37960 hides dyed¦37961 red¦37961 to go over the tent¦37958, then¦37956 another covering sea-cow hides¦37959 to¦37965 go over that.
\s2 The wooden frames
\rem /s1 The Framework
\p
\v 15 You¦37968 must¦37968 make¦37968 frames¦37971 for¦37972 \add &my\add* residence¦37972 from acacia¦37974 wood¦37973. They'll stand¦37975 upright¦37975
\v 16 \add and\add* each one¦37986 must¦37977 be¦37981 five metres¦37978 high and 0.75m wide¦37984.
\v 17 Each¦37993 frame must¦37990 have two¦37988 protrusions so¦37997 it can be connected to the¦37990 frame¦37990 next to it.
\v 18 Assemble¦38004 twenty¦38008 frames¦38006 for¦38007 the¦38010 south¦38011 side¦38010 of¦38011 the residence
\v 19 along with forty¦38014 silver¦38017 bases to go underneath¦38019 them—two bases supporting each frame, and¦38014 each frame¦38021 having two¦38022 protrusions at the bottom to go into the bases¦38031.
\v 20 For¦38039 the¦38039 north¦38043 side¦38039, assemble twenty¦38044 frames¦38045
\v 21 along with forty¦38047 silver¦38049 bases—two under¦38052 each frame¦38053.
\v 22 For¦38061 the¦38061 rear of¦38061 the¦38062 residence¦38062 facing west¦38063, assemble six¦38065 frames¦38066
\v 23 plus two¦38068 extra frames¦38069 for¦38071 \add bracing\add* the¦38071 two back corners¦38071—
\v 24 they¦38075 must¦38075 be¦38075 joined \add on\add* at the¦38086 bottom¦38077 and¦38075 then¦38075 both¦38091 of¦38091 them¦38090 have their¦38090 tops attached to¦38077 a ring¦38086.
\v 25 Then¦38095 assemble eight¦38096 frames¦38097 with their¦38098 sixteen silver¦38099 bases—two bases supporting each frame¦38097.
\p
\v 26 Make¦38114 crossbars from acacia¦38117 wood¦38116—five¦38118 of¦38116 them to¦38119 go across the¦38119 frames¦38119 on the¦38120 northern side¦38120,
\v 27 five for the south side, and¦38125 five for the frames¦38134 at the¦38135 rear of¦38135 the¦38136 residence¦38136 on¦38138 the western¦38138 side.
\v 28 The¦38140 middle¦38141 crossbar in¦38142 the¦38142 centre of¦38143 the¦38143 frames¦38143 will¦38144 go¦38144 right through¦38144 from¦38145 one end¦38147 to¦38148 the¦38150 other.
\v 29 Overlay¦38155 the frames¦38154 and the crossbars with gold¦38156, and¦38157 make¦38160 the rings¦38159 for¦38163 holding the¦38167 crossbars with gold¦38168.
\v 30 Then¦38171 you must¦38170 assemble \add &my¦38173\add* residence¦38173 exactly as per the plan¦38174 that¦38175 you¦38176 were¦38176 shown¦38176 on¦38177 the mountain¦38177.
\s2 The curtain
\rem /s1 The Curtain
\p
\v 31 You¦38191 must¦38180 have a skillful¦38189 workman make¦38180 a curtain¦38181 from twisted¦38187 finely-spun linen¦38186, with winged-creatures \add embroidered on them using\add* blue, purple¦38183, and¦38184 scarlet¦38185 thread.
\v 32 Hang¦38195 it¦38195 from gold clips on¦38196 four¦38198 pillars¦38199 made from acacia¦38200 wood overlaid¦38201 with gold on¦38205 four¦38207 silver¦38210 bases¦38208.
\v 33 Hang the¦38215 curtain¦38215 under¦38216 the clips, then¦38212 bring¦38218 the¦38223 box¦38223 that contains the agreement inside¦38220 the curtain. That curtain will¦38212 separate¦38225 for¦38227 you¦38227 between¦38228 the sacred section and¦38212 the \em very\em* sacred interior.\x + \xo 26:33: \xt Heb 6:19; 9:3-5.\x*
\v 34 Install¦38235 the atonement¦38237 platform as the lid on¦38241 the box¦38239 there in¦38241 the¦38241 very sacred¦38241 interior.
\v 35 Set the¦38247 table¦38247 up outside¦38248 the curtain¦38249 on¦38261 the north¦38264 side, with the lampstand¦38252 on¦38255 the south¦38258 side opposite¦38253 the table.
\p
\v 36 Then¦38266 make¦38266 a¦38267 curtain out of¦38272 twisted¦38275 finely-spun linen¦38274 for¦38268 the¦38268 entrance¦38268 of¦38268 the¦38269 tent¦38269. It should be embroidered with blue, purple¦38271 and¦38266 scarlet¦38273 yarn.
\v 37 Make¦38279 five¦38281 pillars¦38282 for¦38280 the curtain from acacia¦38283 wood overlaid¦38284 with gold¦38286. The hooks¦38287 on them¦38285 must be made¦38279 of¦38282 gold, and¦38279 their¦38287 five¦38291 bases¦38292 must be cast¦38289 with bronze¦38293.
\c 27
\s1 The altar for burnt offerings
