\v 3 \add so\add* speak¦38635 to¦38636 all¦38638 the \add ≈skilled¦38640 craftsmen who've been given¦38644\add* the spirit¦38645 of¦38650 wisdom¦38646, and¦38634 they¦38647 can make¦38647 Aharon's¦38648 clothes¦38650 to¦38652 \add ≈dedicate¦38652 him¦38652 as¦38653\add* my priest¦38653.
\v 4 These¦38657 are¦38658 the¦38658 clothes that¦38659 they'll¦38660 need to make¦38660: a small pouch to hang around the neck and¦38662 an¦38662 apron¦38662, a robe¦38663 and¦38664 a tunic¦38664 of¦38664 woven work¦38665, and a turban¦38666 and¦38667 a waistband¦38667. They¦38668 must¦38660 make¦38668 \add those\add* sacred¦38671 clothes for¦38672 your brother¦38673 Aharon¦38672 and¦38674 for¦38674 his¦38674 sons¦38674 to¦38675 serve¦38675 as¦38675 my priests¦38675.
\v 5 \add @The¦38683 skilled¦38683 craftsmen¦38683\add* must¦38680 \add ≈be given\add* gold¦38683 \add wire\add* and blue, purple¦38689, and¦38690 scarlet¦38692 yarn, and¦38694 finely-spun linen¦38696.
