\v 11 A¦38783 stone¦38771 craftsman with experience at making¦38787 signet rings should do the engravings¦38770, and then mount the two¦38777 stones¦38778 in decorative gold¦38786 settings¦38785.
\v 12 Then¦38790 attach the¦38793 two¦38793 stones¦38794 to the¦38796 shoulder¦38796 pieces of¦38807 the apron as a reminder about¦38793 Yisra'el's¦38801 sons¦38800. That way Aharon¦38803 will¦38802 carry¦38802 their¦38806 names¦38806 on¦38809 his¦38812 two shoulders¦38812 as a reminder \add every time\add* he¦38802 goes to¦38807 face¦38807 Yahweh¦38808.
\v 13 Make¦38816 the decorative settings¦38817 for the \add two\add* stones from gold¦38818,
\v 14 and¦38829 then¦38820 make¦38825 two¦38820 twisted¦38824 chains¦38821 of¦38820 pure¦38823 gold¦38822 like a cord that you¦38825 can attach to the¦38832 decorative settings¦38836.
\s1 The chestpiece
\rem /s1 Design of the Chestpiece; The Breastpiece; The Breastplate
\r (Exo. 39:8-21)
\p
\v 15 Make¦38839 a \bd sacred chest pouch\bd* for \add ≈important decision¦38841 making\add*. A skilled¦38843 craftsman should make¦38846 it¦38846 from twisted¦38853 finely-spun linen¦38852 like¦38844 the¦38842 apron¦38845, embroidered with gold¦38847 \add wire\add* and¦38849 blue, purple¦38849, and¦38850 scarlet¦38851 yarn.
\v 16 It¦38858 needs to be¦38858 23cm square¦38857 when folded¦38859 over double¦38859,
\v 17 and¦38865 it¦38866 will¦38872 have four¦38869 rows¦38870 of¦38872 \add three\add* gemstones¦38871 on it: a \add red\add* ruby¦38873, a \add yellow\add* topaz¦38874, a \add green\add* emerald¦38875,
\v 18 then¦38879 a turquoise¦38881, a \add blue\add* sapphire¦38882, a diamond¦38883,
\v 19 then¦38885 a \add red\add* jacinth¦38887, a \add white\add* agate¦38888, a \add purple\add* amethyst¦38889,
\v 20 and¦38891 in the¦38891 last row¦38891, a \add yellow\add* beryl, an¦38894 onyx¦38894, and¦38895 a \add green\add* jasper¦38895. All those stones must¦38893 be¦38898 mounted¦38899 in decorative gold¦38897 settings¦38899,
\v 21 and¦38901 \add so\add* they'll¦38902 represent the twelve tribes¦38923 of Yisrael¦38908. The¦38906 names¦38919 of the twelve sons¦38906 must¦38902 be¦38920 engraved¦38914 on¦38903 the stones¦38901 similar to how signet rings \add are made\add*.
\v 22 Make¦38925 two twisted¦38930 chains¦38929 of¦38929 pure¦38934 gold¦38933 like a cord that you¦38925 can attach to the¦38928 pouch,
\v 23 then¦38936 make¦38936 two¦38940 gold¦38942 rings¦38941 and¦38936 attach them to the two¦38946 \add top\add* corners of¦38946 the pouch.
\v 24 Attach¦38955 the two¦38957 gold¦38959 chains to¦38964 the rings¦38963 on¦38960 the corners
\v 25 with the other ends¦38971 fastened to the¦38972 two¦38972 decorative settings¦38978 \add around the stones\add* and¦38969 then¦38969 attached to¦38984 the¦38986 front¦38986 side of¦38977 the shoulder¦38982 straps.
\v 26 Make¦38994 two more gold¦38992 rings¦38991 and¦38989 attach them¦38994 on¦38995 the inside¦39008 to¦39004 the¦39006 two \add bottom\add* corners of¦39006 the pouch,
\v 27 and¦39010 another two¦39011 gold¦39013 rings¦39012 to be attached to the bottom of¦39011 the¦39018 two¦39018 shoulder¦39019 pieces near¦39024 where the shoulder straps join¦39025 the apron just above¦39026 the¦39027 crafted waistband¦39027.
\v 28 Then¦39031 tie¦39030 the¦39033 rings¦39034 on the sacred pouch to¦39036 the¦39038 rings¦39038 on the¦39039 apron¦39039 with¦39040 a blue cord¦39040 so that the pouch sits above the waistband¦39045 and¦39047 can't¦39047 come loose from¦39051 the¦39052 apron¦39052.
\p
\v 29 Then¦39054 \add whenever\add* Aharon¦39055 enters the sacred inner room¦39070 \add to stand\add* in¦39062 front¦39072 of \add *me\add*, he'll¦39054 be carrying¦39054 the¦39058 names¦39058 of Yisra'el's¦39061 sons¦39059 over¦39064 his¦39066 heart¦39066 on¦39062 the sacred pouch that'll be used for making decisions¦39063.
\v 30 Then¦39077 place¦39077 the ‘Urim¦39084’ and¦39077 the ‘Tummim’\f + \fr 28:30 \ft These two objects appear abruptly in the text—they haven't been described previously—in fact, they're not described anywhere, so we don't really know much about them except that it seems they were used somehow to indicate Yahweh's decision on important matters. Although we presume that Mosheh must have already been familiar with them, sadly we're unable to translate these two Hebrew words, because we're not.\f* in the sacred pouch so they'll¦39088 be¦39088 over¦39089 Aharon's¦39092 heart when¦39093 he¦39093 goes¦39093 in¦39094 before¦39094 Yahweh, thus Aharon¦39097 will¦39096 continually¦39109 bear¦39096 the¦39100 decisions of¦39100 the¦39101 Israelis¦39103 over¦39104 his¦39106 heart¦39106 before¦39107 Yahweh.\x + \xo 28:30: \xt Num 27:21; Deu 33:8; Ezr 2:63; Neh 7:65.\x*
\s1 The other parts of the uniform
\rem /s1 Additional Clothing for the Priests; Other Priestly Vestments; Other Priestly Garments; The Other Priestly Garments
