\r (Lev. 8:1-36)
\p
\v 1 Now this¦39336 is¦39337 how you¦39340 should consecrate¦39342 them¦39341 to be¦39337 priests¦39344 to¦39345 me¦39345: Take¦39346 a young¦39347 bull¦39347 from the¦39351 herd¦39351 and¦39352 two¦39353 rams¦39352 without¦39354 defects¦39354.
\v 2 \add Also,\add* using finely-ground wheat¦39367 flour¦39366, \add bake\add* flat bread¦39356, flat¦39357 cakes¦39358 with¦39361 \add olive\add* oil in¦39361 them¦39369, and¦39356 flat wafers¦39362 sprinkled with¦39365 \add olive\add* oil¦39365.
\v 3 Put¦39371 \add @the¦39372 baking¦39372\add* into a¦39375 basket¦39375, and¦39377 bring¦39377 the basket \add to me\add* along with¦39379 the¦39382 bull¦39382 and¦39383 two¦39384 rams¦39385.
\p
\v 4 Then¦39387 take¦39393 Aharon¦39389 and¦39390 his¦39392 sons¦39392 near¦39393 to¦39394 the¦39396 entrance¦39396 of¦39396 the¦39397 sacred¦39397 tent¦39397 and¦39399 wash¦39399 them¦39400 with¦39401 water¦39401.
\v 5 Take¦39403 the¦39406 clothes¦39407 and dress¦39407 Aharon¦39410 in¦39425 the tunic¦39413 and¦39414 the¦39415 robe¦39415 that goes with¦39425 the apron, then¦39403 the sacred apron and the sacred pouch, and tie the waistband¦39425 around the apron¦39426.
\v 6 Put¦39434 the turban¦39429 on¦39430 his¦39432 head¦39432 and¦39433 attach the sacred¦39437 \add gold\add* ornament to it,
\v 7 then¦39442 take¦39442 the¦39445 anointing¦39446 oil¦39445 and¦39442 pour¦39447 it¦39452 over his¦39450 head¦39450 to dedicate him¦39452.
\v 8 \add Next,\add* bring¦39457 his¦39456 sons¦39456 and¦39458 put tunics¦39459 on them¦39458
\v 9 and¦39461 wrap waistbands around them¦39462 and¦39466 tie¦39466 on¦39466 their headbands. They¦39462 \add and their descendants\add* will¦39469 be priests¦39471 forever¦39473, and¦39474 you¦39474 must¦39461 ordain¦39474 \add both\add* Aharon¦39464 and¦39465 his¦39465 sons¦39480.
\p
\v 10 Then¦39482 bring¦39482 the¦39485 bull¦39485 to¦39486 the¦39486 front¦39486 of¦39486 the¦39487 sacred¦39487 tent¦39487 and¦39489 get Aharon¦39490 and¦39491 his¦39491 sons¦39491 to put their¦39494 hands¦39494 on¦39495 its head¦39497,
\v 11 then¦39500 slaughter¦39500\f + \fr 29:11 \ft The throat will be cut with a sharp knife, and the blood will be caught in a bowl.\f* the¦39503 bull¦39503 before¦39504 \add *me¦39505\add* at the¦39506 entrance¦39506 of¦39506 the¦39507 sacred¦39507 tent¦39507.
\v 12 Take¦39519 some¦39511 of¦39511 that blood¦39511 and¦39510 smear it on¦39514 the¦39516 top projections of¦39516 the¦39517 altar¦39517 with¦39518 your¦39518 finger¦39518, then¦39510 pour¦39524 the rest of it \add on the ground\add* at¦39518 the base¦39527 of¦39527 the¦39528 altar¦39528.
\v 13 Take¦39530 all¦39533 the¦39535 fat¦39535 covering¦39536 the¦39539 innards¦39539 including¦39540 the¦39541 lobe¦39541 above the¦39544 liver¦39544, as well as both¦39546 kidneys¦39547 and¦39548 the¦39550 fat¦39550 on¦39552 them¦39552, and¦39553 burn¦39553 it all on the¦39554 altar¦39554,
\v 14 but¦39556 the¦39558 bull's meat¦39558 and¦39560 hide¦39562 and¦39563 intestines must¦39566 be¦39570 burnt¦39566 outside¦39568 the camp¦39569. Sacrificing¦39570 \add the bull's fat like that\add* is¦39570 an act of¦39558 purification.
\p
\v 15 Then¦39573 take¦39577 one¦39576 of¦39580 the¦39586 rams and have Aharon¦39579 and¦39580 his¦39580 sons¦39580 place¦39578 their¦39583 hands¦39583 on¦39584 \add *its¦39586\add* head¦39586,
\v 16 then¦39589 slaughter¦39589 it. \add Catch\add* the¦39592 blood¦39596 and¦39589 sprinkle¦39597 it all¦39601 over \add the sides of\add* the altar¦39600.
\v 17 Then¦39603 cut¦39606 the ram¦39605 into¦39607 pieces¦39607 and¦39608 wash¦39608 its innards¦39609 and its legs¦39610, and¦39611 put¦39611 \add @those¦39611 bits¦39611\add* \add together\add* with¦39612 the head¦39617 and the \add other\add* pieces.
\v 18 Then¦39619 burn¦39619 \add *it¦39627\add* all¦39622 on the altar¦39625. That will¦39619 be¦39626 a burnt¦39626 offering to¦39625 \add *me¦39628\add*—a pleasing¦39630 aroma¦39629 \add from\add* the offering by fire¦39631.\x + \xo 29:18: \xt Eph 5:2; Php 4:18.\x*
\p
\v 19 Then¦39635 take¦39635 the¦39637 second¦39638 ram¦39637, and¦39639 have Aharon¦39640 and¦39641 his¦39641 sons¦39641 place¦39639 their¦39644 hands¦39644 on¦39645 \add *its¦39647\add* head¦39647,
\v 20 then¦39650 slaughter¦39650 it. \add Catch\add* the¦39653 blood¦39655 and smear some¦39655 of¦39655 it on¦39657 the tip of Aharon¦39661 and¦39662 his¦39666 sons¦39666' right¦39667 ears and¦39668 on¦39668 their right thumbs¦39670 and¦39673 big¦39675 toes¦39675. Then¦39650 sprinkle¦39678 the rest all¦39685 over \add the sides of\add* the altar¦39684.
\v 21 Take¦39687 some¦39688 of¦39688 the¦39690 blood¦39690 that¦39691 is¦39692 on¦39692 the¦39694 altar¦39694 and¦39695 some¦39695 of¦39695 the anointing¦39696 oil¦39695, and¦39697 sprinkle¦39697 that on Aharon and his clothes, and on his sons¦39710 and¦39712 their clothes. That will¦39712 consecrate¦39712 Aharon and¦39714 his¦39714 sons¦39715 and¦39716 their \add priestly\add* clothes.
\p
\v 22 Take¦39720 the fat of¦39735 \add that second\add* ram, and its fat tail¦39725, the¦39728 fat¦39728 covering¦39730 its innards¦39733 and¦39734 the¦39735 lobe¦39735 above the¦39736 liver¦39736, the¦39739 two¦39739 kidneys¦39740 and¦39741 that fat¦39743 that's¦39744 on¦39745 them¦39745, and¦39746 the right¦39748 thigh¦39747, \add because\add* this ram is¦39745 for¦39749 consecration.
\v 23 \add Also\add* take one \add round\add* bread loaf¦39754, one¦39756 cake¦39757 of¦39757 bread¦39758 made with oil¦39759 in¦39766 it, and¦39754 one¦39760 wafer¦39761 from¦39763 that¦39765 basket¦39763 of¦39763 flat¦39764 breads¦39764 that's¦39765 \add offered to\add* \add *me¦39767\add*.
\v 24 Put¦39781 all those into the¦39770 hands of¦39772 Aharon¦39773 and¦39774 his¦39776 sons¦39776, and \add they\add* must¦39769 wave¦39777 them¦39778 before¦39780 \add *me¦39781\add* as a wave offering.
\v 25 Then¦39783 take¦39783 them¦39784 from¦39785 their¦39785 hands¦39785 and¦39786 burn¦39786 them¦39786 completely on the¦39787 altar¦39787 on¦39788 top of¦39791 the burnt¦39790 offering. That also¦39786 will¦39786 be¦39795 a fire¦39795 offering¦39795 to¦39797 \add *me\add*, and its aroma¦39791 will please \add *me\add*.
\p
\v 26 Take¦39811 the breast¦39802 meat of the¦39803 ram¦39803 (\add the second one\add* for¦39813 the consecration of Aharon¦39806) and wave it as a wave offering¦39804 before¦39810 \add *me\add*. Then¦39799 after that¦39805 it will¦39799 be¦39812 your share¦39814 \add to cook and eat\add*.
\p
\v 27 \add So\add* you¦39816 should consecrate¦39816 the¦39819 breast¦39819 of¦39819 the¦39820 wave¦39825 offering¦39820 and¦39821 the¦39822 thigh¦39822 of¦39822 the¦39823 contribution¦39823 from¦39828 the¦39828 ram¦39828 of consecration¦39816 for Aharon¦39831 and his¦39833 sons¦39833.
\v 28 Those will belong to¦39836 Aharon¦39836 and¦39835 his¦39837 sons¦39837 as their regular portion¦39838 from¦39841 the¦39842 Israelis¦39843—it will¦39848 be¦39848 a contribution¦39845 from¦39849 the¦39850 Israelis¦39852 from¦39853 their¦39854 peace¦39854 offerings¦39854 to¦39856 \add *me¦39856\add*.
\p
\v 29 The¦39870 sacred¦39859 clothes¦39858 that¦39860 belong¦39862 to Aharon¦39861 will¦39862 be used for¦39865 his¦39863 male descendants¦39863 to wear \add in turn\add* when they're anointed¦39865 and¦39858 consecrated.
\v 30 The¦39877 priest¦39877 who succeeds¦39878 him¦39878 from among his¦39878 sons¦39879, who¦39880 comes¦39881 into¦39882 the¦39884 sacred tent¦39887 to¦39886 serve¦39886 in¦39887 the sacred inner room¦39878 must¦39876 wear¦39876 them¦39876 for seven¦39874 days¦39875.
\p
