\v 1 \add Meanwhile,\add* the¦41002 people¦41002 had noticed¦41001 that¦41003 Mosheh¦41006 \add ≈had been up¦41034 on the mountain¦41010 for a long time\add*, \add so\add* \add *they¦41016\add* gathered¦41011 themselves around Aharon¦41015 and¦41001 told¦41016 him¦41017, “Come¦41007 on. Make¦41020 \add +some\add* gods¦41023 for us that can go¦41025 ahead¦41026 of us, because¦41003 we¦41038 don't¦41037 know¦41038 what's¦41039 happened¦41041 to¦41007 that Mosheh¦41031—the¦41032 man¦41032\f + \fr 32:1 \ft The way that the people speak of Mosheh here suggests that maybe they never really ever regarded him as being one of them—remember, he did grow up in an Egyptian palace.\f* who¦41033 brought¦41034 us¦41034 out of¦41035 Egypt¦41036.”\x + \xo 32:1: \xt Acts 7:40.\x*
