\v 4 and he¦41075 took¦41073 them and smelted and crafted the gold into the form of a young bull. Then¦41073 \add @the people\add* said¦41081, “These¦41082 are¦41083 your¦41083 gods¦41083,\f + \fr 32:4 \ft After crafting the gold into the form of a young bull (which wasn't necessarily solid but may have had an internal wooden frame or a clay centre), it's not clear here why the text refers to plural ‘gods’.\f* Yisrael¦41084, who¦41085 brought¦41086 you¦41086 out of¦41087 Egypt¦41088.”\x + \xo 32:4: \xt 1Ki 12:28; Acts 7:41.\x*
\p
\v 5 \add ≈When¦41090\add* Aharon¦41091 saw¦41090 \add <that\add*, he¦41097 built¦41092 an¦41093 altar¦41093 in front¦41094 of the bull and¦41090 announced, “Tomorrow¦41096 will¦41100 be¦41100 a festival¦41098 to¦41099 \add honour\add* Yahweh¦41099.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦41102\add* they¦41102 got up early¦41102 the¦41103 next¦41103 day¦41103 and¦41104 offered¦41104 burnt¦41105 offerings¦41105 and¦41106 brought¦41106 peace¦41107 offerings. Then¦41102 the¦41109 people¦41109 sat¦41108 down¦41108 to¦41110 eat¦41110 and¦41111 drink¦41111, then¦41102 stood up¦41104 to \add ≈make merry\add*.\x + \xo 32:6: \xt 1Cor 10:7.\x*
\p
\v 7 Then Yahweh¦41117 \add ≈told¦41116\add* Mosheh¦41120, “Go¦41121 on down¦41123 because¦41124 your¦41126 people¦41126 that¦41127 you¦41128 brought¦41128 out of¦41126 Egypt¦41130 have¦41125 gone bad—
\v 8 they've quickly¦41133 deviated from¦41134 what I¦41138 instructed¦41138 them¦41138. They've¦41132 made¦41139 a¦41141 metal¦41142 bull for¦41140 themselves and¦41143 have¦41143 bowed¦41143 down¦41143 to¦41145 it¦41145 and¦41146 sacrificed¦41146 to¦41148 it¦41148 and¦41149 they've said¦41149, ‘Yisrael¦41152, these¦41150 are¦41151 your¦41151 gods¦41151 that¦41137 brought¦41154 you¦41154 out of¦41155 Egypt¦41156.’ ”
\v 9 Then¦41158 Yahweh¦41159 said¦41158 to¦41160 Mosheh¦41162, “I've¦41163 seen¦41163 this¦41167 people¦41169, and¦41158 look, \add ≈they're so stubborn\add*.
\v 10 \add So\add* leave¦41177 me¦41178 alone¦41177 now¦41176 and let my¦41181 anger¦41181 rage against them¦41182. I¦41185 will¦41184 destroy¦41183 them¦41183 and¦41184 make¦41184 you¦41185 into¦41186 a¦41186 great¦41187 nation¦41186.”
\v 11 But¦41189 Mosheh¦41190 pleaded with his¦41195 god¦41195 Yahweh and¦41196 \add ≈asked¦41196\add*, “Yahweh, why¦41197 \add ≈are you angry¦41200 at¦41201\add* your people¦41201 that¦41202 you¦41203 have brought¦41203 out¦41203 of¦41204 Egypt¦41205 with¦41206 \add ≈your incredible¦41207 power¦41206 and¦41208 actions\add*?\x + \xo 32:11-14: \xt Num 14:13-19.\x*
