\v 16 He¦44166 \add also\add* made¦44166 the¦44169 utensils¦44169 that¦44171 would be¦44172 on¦44188 the table¦44174—its plates¦44177 and¦44178 pans¦44180, and its bowls¦44182 and¦44183 pitchers¦44185 to be¦44187 used for pouring¦44187 out¦44187 \add <the wine offerings\add*—all made from pure¦44190 gold¦44189.
\s1 Making the lampstand
\rem /s1 Building the Lampstand; The Lampstand; Making the Lampstand
\r (Exo. 25:31-40)
\p
\v 17 Then he¦44193 made¦44193 the¦44196 lampstand from¦44209 pure¦44198 gold¦44197. The¦44203 base¦44204 and¦44205 shaft¦44205 of¦44204 the lampstand were¦44210 hammered¦44199 \add ≈into shape\add*, along with its cups¦44206, and its buds and¦44208 blossoms¦44208.
\v 18 There were¦44214 six¦44212 branches¦44213 going¦44214 out¦44214 from¦44215 the¦44221 shaft of¦44223 the lampstand—three on each side¦44215.
\v 19 Each branch¦44231 had three¦44235 gold cups¦44236 on¦44231 it that¦44245 looked like¦44230 almond¦44237 flowers with¦44231 buds and¦44234 petals. It was¦44238 the same for¦44243 each of¦44243 the lampstand's¦44248 six¦44243 branches¦44244.
\v 20 On¦44250 the lampstand¦44250 \add shaft\add* there were¦44250 four¦44251 cups¦44252 that also¦44255 looked like¦44253 almond¦44253 blossoms¦44253, each one with¦44250 flower buds and¦44250 petals¦44255.
\v 21 He made one flower bud beneath¦44258 every pair of¦44259 branches¦44260 \add (that were going out from opposite sides)\add*. The¦44265 bud was¦44268 attached to each pair of¦44270 branches¦44271 as if they were growing out of it¦44272—all six¦44273 lampstand branches¦44274 were attached like that¦44275.
\v 22 The buds and¦44279 the branches¦44279 coming out of¦44279 them were¦44281 all¦44282 hammered¦44283 out of one¦44284 piece of pure¦44286 gold¦44285.
\v 23 Then¦44289 he¦44288 made¦44288 the seven¦44292 lamps¦44291 out of¦44291 pure¦44296 gold¦44295, along with the tongs¦44293 and¦44288 trays¦44294.
\v 24 He¦44301 made¦44301 \add @the¦44301 lampstand¦44301\add* and tongs and trays using 33kg of¦44304 pure¦44300 gold¦44299.
\s1 Making the incense altar
\rem /s1 Building the Incense Altar; Making the Altar of Incense; Making the Altar for Burning Incense
\r (Exo. 30:1-5)
\p
\v 25 Then he¦44309 made¦44309 the¦44312 altar¦44312 \add for burning\add* incense¦44313 out of¦44314 acacia¦44315 wood¦44314. It¦44309 was¦44316 square¦44320—half a metre on each side—and¦44321 one metre high¦44322. Its¦44317 projections \add on the top four corners\add* were¦44324 part of it¦44323.
\v 26 He¦44327 overlaid¦44327 it¦44328 with pure¦44330 gold—all four sides¦44336 including¦44334 the projections—and¦44327 put a gold¦44329 moulding¦44343 all¦44345 around¦44345 it.
\v 27 Then¦44365 he¦44350 made¦44350 two gold¦44349 rings¦44348 \add and attached them\add* below the moulding¦44355—two on¦44366 each side¦44358 for holding the poles¦44363 for carrying¦44364 \add @the¦44350 altar¦44350\add*.
\v 28 The¦44371 \add two\add* poles¦44371 were made¦44368 from acacia¦44373 wood¦44372 and¦44374 then¦44368 overlaid¦44374 with gold¦44376.
\rem /s1 Making the Anointing Oil and the Incense
\rem /r (Exodus 30.22-38)
\v 29 He¦44378 got a \add professional\add* ointment maker¦44378 to make¦44378 the sacred¦44383 anointing¦44382 oil¦44381 and¦44384 the pure¦44383, fragrant¦44387 incense¦44386.\x + \xo 37:29: \xt Exo 30:22-38.\x*
\c 38
