\rem /s1 The Altar of Burnt Offering; Building the Altar of Burnt Offering; Making the Altar for Burning Offerings; Making the Altar of Burnt Offering
\r (Exo. 27:1-8)
\p
\v 1 Then \add @Bezalel¦44393\add* made¦44393 the¦44396 altar¦44396 for burning¦44397 offerings¦44397 from acacia¦44399 wood¦44398. It¦44393 was¦44400 square¦44407—2.5m on each side—and¦44408 1.5m tall.
\v 2 \add ≈From¦44421 the same piece of wood\add*, he made¦44412 horn-like projections for each of¦44413 the¦44415 four¦44415 corners¦44416, then¦44412 he overlaid¦44420 it¦44421 all with bronze¦44422.
\v 3 He¦44424 made¦44424 all¦44427 the utensils¦44448 for the altar¦44430: the¦44433 pots¦44433 and¦44434 shovels¦44436, basins¦44439 and meat-forks, and the¦44445 firepans¦44445—all¦44446 made¦44449 from bronze¦44450.
\v 4 He¦44452 made¦44452 a grating¦44454 for¦44453 the altar¦44453—a bronze¦44457 lattice \add that fitted\add* \add ≈down in the middle¦44463 of¦44455 the altar\add*,
\v 5 and¦44465 he¦44465 cast¦44465 the grating¦44470 with¦44468 rings¦44467 on¦44468 the¦44468 four¦44468 corners¦44469 as holders¦44472 for¦44470 the \add carrying\add* poles¦44473.
\v 6 He¦44475 made¦44475 the¦44478 acacia¦44480 wood¦44479 poles¦44478 and¦44481 overlaid¦44481 them¦44482 with bronze¦44483
\v 7 and¦44485 he¦44485 put the¦44488 poles¦44488 into¦44489 the rings¦44489 on¦44489 the¦44491 sides¦44491 of¦44491 the¦44492 altar¦44492 so they could carry¦44493 it¦44494 with¦44489 them¦44495. He¦44498 made¦44498 \add @the altar\add* hollow¦44496 using boards¦44497.
\s1 Making the washbasin
\rem /s1 Basin for Washing; Building the Washbasin; Making the Bronze Basin
\r (Exo. 30:18)
\p
\v 8 Then he¦44502 made¦44502 a bronze¦44505 washbasin and¦44506 base¦44507. \add They were made\add* with¦44509 the bronze from the mirrors¦44509 of¦44509 the¦44510 serving¦44510 women¦44510 who¦44511 served¦44512 at¦44509 the entrance¦44513 of¦44513 the¦44514 sacred¦44514 tent¦44514.\x + \xo 38:8: \xt Exo 30:18.\x*
\s1 Making the courtyard
\rem /s1 Making the Court of the Tabernacle; The Enclosure for the Tent of the Lord's Presence; The Courtyard; Building the Courtyard
\r (Exo. 27:9-19)
\p
\v 9 Then \add @Bezalel¦44518\add* worked on¦44531 the courtyard. For¦44522 the south¦44524 side¦44522, the courtyard curtains¦44526 were¦44528 fifty metres¦44531 of¦44522 twisted¦44529 finely-spun linen¦44528
\v 10 with their¦44533 twenty¦44534 \add bronze\add* pillars and¦44535 their bases¦44535. The¦44538 hooks¦44538 on the¦44539 pillars¦44539 and¦44540 their rings¦44540 were¦44541 made of¦44533 silver¦44541.
\v 11 On the¦44543 north¦44544 side¦44543, there were¦44548 fifty metres¦44546 of¦44549 curtains with¦44546 their twenty¦44550 bronze¦44551 pillars¦44553 and bases¦44549, and their¦44554 silver¦44555 hooks¦44552 and rings¦44554.
\v 12 On the¦44557 west¦44559 side¦44557, there were¦44564 twenty-five metres¦44562 of¦44565 curtains¦44560 with¦44562 their ten¦44566 pillars¦44568 and bases¦44565, and their¦44569 silver¦44570 hooks¦44567 and rings¦44569,
\v 13 and¦44572 \add another\add* twenty-five metres on the¦44572 east side¦44572.
\v 14 The¦44585 curtains¦44578 for \add one\add* side¦44585 \add of the entrance\add* were¦44587 7.5m long with their¦44588 three¦44589 pillars¦44586 and¦44588 their bases¦44588.
\v 15 On the \add ≈other\add* side¦44591, opposite the courtyard¦44596 entrance¦44595, the curtains¦44597 were¦44598 7.5m long with their three¦44602 pillars¦44601 and¦44591 their bases¦44603.
\v 16 All¦44606 of¦44606 the¦44608 courtyard¦44609 curtains¦44608 were¦44611 made with twisted¦44612 finely-spun linen¦44611.
\v 17 The¦44614 bases¦44614 for¦44615 the pillars¦44615 were¦44616 bronze¦44616, \add ≈but¦44614\add* the¦44617 hooks¦44617 on them and¦44614 their¦44619 rings were¦44620 silver. All¦44627 of¦44627 the courtyard¦44629 pillars had decorative silver caps fitted to their tops¦44622.
\v 18 The¦44631 curtain for the¦44632 courtyard gate¦44632 was done by an embroiderer. It was made¦44634 from twisted¦44641 finely-spun linen¦44640 \add embroidered\add* with¦44646 blue, purple¦44637, and¦44638 scarlet¦44639 yard. The curtain was¦44647 ten metres¦44648 long¦44644 and¦44645 2.5m high¦44645, just like¦44649 the¦44650 other courtyard curtains¦44650
\v 19 with its four¦44654 bronze¦44657 pillars¦44653 and their bases¦44655 and their¦44655 silver hooks¦44658 and rings¦44662, and with silver¦44663 caps.
\v 20 All¦44665 the¦44667 tent¦44667 pegs¦44667 for¦44668 the sacred¦44668 tent and¦44669 for¦44669 around¦44670 the courtyard¦44669 were¦44671 made with bronze¦44671.
\s1 List of metals used
\rem /s1 The Materials Used; Materials of the Tabernacle; Metals Used in the Tent of the Lord's Presence; Inventory of Materials
\p
\v 21 These¦44674 are¦44675 the records¦44680 \add from making\add* the sacred tent¦44676 (where the \add stone\add* transcripts¦44678 were kept). They were recorded¦44680 by the Levites¦44686 according to Mosheh's¦44684 instructions \add and supervised by\add* Ithamar¦44688 (a son¦44689 of¦44687 Aharon¦44691 the¦44692 priest¦44692).
\p
\v 22 Bezalel (son¦44695 of¦44695 Uri¦44697 son¦44698 of¦44698 Hur¦44700, from the¦44701 tribe¦44701 of Judah¦44702) made¦44703 everything that¦44707 Yahweh¦44710 had¦44709 instructed¦44709 Mosheh¦44713 \add <to make\add*.
\v 23 Oholiab¦44716 (son¦44717 of¦44717 Ahisamak¦44719, from the¦44720 tribe¦44720 of Dan¦44722) worked with¦44726 him¦44715—he was¦44715 an¦44723 engraver¦44723 and¦44724 a designer¦44724 and¦44725 an embroiderer¦44725 in blue, purple¦44727, and¦44728 scarlet¦44728, and¦44730 in¦44730 fine linen¦44730.
\p
\v 24 The¦44735 gold¦44735 that¦44736 they used¦44736 for¦44737 the¦44739 construction of¦44739 the¦44740 sacred¦44740 tent was measured at¦44738 965kg. This was¦44741 the¦44743 gold¦44743 from the¦44744 wave offering¦44744 and¦44746 was weighed using¦44736 the official standard weights.
\v 25 The¦44755 silver¦44755 contributed by¦44766 the people was¦44758 measured at¦44766 3,420kg \add also\add* using the official weights.\x + \xo 38:25-26: \xt Exo 30:11-16.\x*
\v 26 \add During the census,\add* every¦44775 male who¦44776 was twenty¦44781 years¦44782 old or older paid a 5g silver coin—a total of¦44771 603,550 men.\x + \xo 38:26: \xt Mat 17:24.\x*
\v 27 They'd used 3,400kg of silver¦44797 to¦44798 make the¦44800 bases¦44800 under the pillars that supported the sacred¦44801 tent's curtains¦44804 (34kg for¦44807 each of one¦44795 hundred¦44805 bases¦44806)
\v 28 and¦44812 the¦44814 other twenty kilograms were used for the¦44816 hooks¦44820 for¦44821 the pillars¦44821 and¦44822 for the caps on the tops¦44823 of¦44823 them¦44825.
\v 29 The¦44827 bronze¦44827 from the¦44828 wave offering¦44828 came to 2,400kg
\v 30 and¦44837 it¦44837 was used to¦44854 make¦44837 the¦44841 bases¦44841 \add for the pillars\add* at¦44838 the tent¦44843 entrance¦44842 and¦44845 for the¦44846 altar¦44846 and¦44848 its grating¦44850 and¦44855 all¦44856 the¦44858 utensils¦44858,
\v 31 and¦44861 for the¦44863 bases¦44863 \add for the posts\add* for \add the curtains\add* around the¦44864 courtyard¦44864 and¦44866 at the entrance¦44869, and¦44871 for the tent¦44875 pegs¦44880 for the \add ≈main structure\add* and around the courtyard.
\c 39
\s1 Making the priests' uniforms
\rem /s1 Making the Vestments for the Priesthood; The Priestly Garments; Clothing for the Priests; Making the Garments for the Priests
\r (Exo. 28:1-14)
\p
\v 1 They used the blue, purple¦44887, and¦44884 scarlet¦44888 \add cloth\add* to make the¦44889 sacred clothes to¦44894 be used in¦44895 the sacred tent¦44895. They made¦44890 Aharon's¦44902 clothes just¦44903 as¦44903 Yahweh¦44905 had¦44904 instructed¦44904 Mosheh¦44908.
\s2 The sacred apron
\rem /s1 The Ephod; Making the Ephod
\p
\v 2 \add @Bezalel¦44911\add* made¦44911 the¦44914 sacred apron¦44914 from twisted¦44921 finely-spun linen¦44920 \add embroidered with\add* gold¦44915 \add wire\add*, and¦44917 blue, purple¦44917, and¦44918 scarlet¦44919 yarn.
\v 3 They¦44924 hammered¦44923 thin¦44926 sheets of¦44926 gold¦44927 and¦44928 he¦44928 cut¦44928 them¦44928 into thread¦44929 of wire for¦44930 a skillful¦44941 craftsman to \add ≈embroider\add* into the fine¦44939 linen¦44939 along with¦44933 the¦44934 blue, purple¦44934, and¦44935 scarlet¦44936 yarn.
\v 4 They¦44944 made¦44944 joined shoulder pieces for it¦44946—joined¦44947 on¦44948 two¦44950 corners
\v 5 and¦44955 the¦44955 skillfully¦44955 woven¦44955 waistband¦44955 which¦44957 is attached to the apron was made of¦44961 the same material of¦44965 twisted¦44968 finely-spun linen¦44967, and had similar¦44961 embroidery using gold¦44962 \add wire\add*, and¦44964 blue, purple¦44964, and¦44965 scarlet¦44966 yarn, just¦44969 as¦44969 Yahweh¦44971 had instructed¦44970 Mosheh¦44974.
\v 6 They¦44976 cut \add two\add* onyx¦44980 stones¦44979 and¦44976 mounted¦44982 them in decorative gold¦44983 settings¦44982. The¦44979 names¦44989 of the¦44980 \add twelve\add* sons¦44990 of¦44990 Yisra'el¦44991 were engraved on¦44987 \add them\add* similar to how a signet ring is engraved,
\v 7 and¦44993 he¦44993 put¦44993 them¦44994 on¦44995 the¦44996 shoulder¦44996 pieces of¦44996 the¦44997 sacred apron¦44997 as stones¦44998 of¦44998 reminder for¦45000 the¦45000 sons¦45000 of¦45000 Yisra'el¦45001, as¦45002 Yahweh¦45004 had¦45003 instructed¦45003 Mosheh¦45007.
\s1 Making the sacred pouch
\rem /s1 Making the Breastpiece; The Breastpiece; Making the Chestpiece
\r (Exo. 28:15-30)
\p
\v 8 Then he¦45010 made the¦45013 sacred chest pouch which took the¦45014 work¦45014 of¦45014 a skilled¦45015 craftsman like¦45016 making the sacred apron. It¦45010 too was made of twisted¦45024 finely-spun linen¦45023 and embroidered with gold¦45018 \add wire\add*, and¦45020 blue, purple¦45020, and¦45021 scarlet¦45022 yarn.
\v 9 When¦45030 the¦45032 material was folded¦45037 over double¦45037, it¦45027 made¦45029 a¦45033 square¦45026 pouch that was 23cm long¦45034 and¦45035 23cm wide¦45036,
\v 10 and¦45039 they¦45039 attached four¦45042 rows¦45043 of¦45043 gemstones¦45044 onto the¦45049 front. The¦45050 first row¦45045 had a \add red\add* ruby¦45046, a \add yellow\add* topaz¦45047, and¦45048 a \add red\add* garnet.
\v 11 The¦45052 second¦45053 row¦45052 had a \add green\add* emerald¦45056, a \add blue\add* sapphire¦45055, and¦45056 a diamond¦45056.
\v 12 The¦45058 third¦45059 row¦45058 had a \add red\add* jacinth¦45060, a \add white\add* agate¦45061, and¦45062 a \add purple\add* amethyst¦45062.
\v 13 The¦45064 fourth¦45065 row¦45064 had a \add yellow\add* beryl, an¦45067 onyx¦45067, and¦45068 a \add green\add* jasper¦45068. \add @All¦45065 the¦45065 stones¦45065\add* were¦45069 mounted in¦45072 decorative gold¦45071 settings¦45070.
\v 14 The¦45074 gemstones were¦45075 engraved with the¦45077 names¦45077 of¦45077 the¦45078 twelve sons¦45078 of¦45078 Yisra'el¦45080 similar to how a signet ring is engraved, and¦45074 they¦45081 represented the¦45087 twelve tribes¦45095.
\v 15 They¦45097 \add attached two\add* twisted¦45102 chains¦45101 of¦45101 pure¦45106 gold¦45105 crafted like a cord onto the¦45100 pouch,
\v 16 and¦45108 made¦45108 two¦45109 decorative gold settings¦45110 and¦45112 two¦45112 gold¦45114 rings¦45119, and attached them to the \add ≈upper corners\add* of¦45118 the sacred pouch.
\v 17 They¦45126 attached one end¦45136 of each gold¦45129 chain to one of¦45132 the¦45133 rings¦45133 on¦45134 the¦45136 \add ≈top corner\add* of¦45136 the¦45137 pouch,
\v 18 and¦45139 they¦45149 attached¦45149 the other end¦45141 of each chain to¦45154 the two¦45142 decorative settings¦45148 that enclose the stones. Then¦45139 they¦45144 put¦45144 those on¦45145 the front¦45156 side of the shoulder¦45152 straps of¦45152 the¦45153 sacred apron¦45153.
\v 19 Then¦45159 they¦45159 made¦45159 two¦45160 \add more\add* gold¦45162 rings¦45161 and¦45159 attached them¦45163 to the¦45166 \add ≈lower corners\add* of¦45166 the sacred pouch on¦45169 the inside¦45177 edges¦45171 next to¦45173 the sacred apron¦45176.
\v 20 They¦45179 made¦45179 two¦45180 more gold¦45182 rings¦45181 and¦45179 attached¦45183 them¦45183 to¦45189 the lower¦45189 part of the¦45190 front¦45190 of¦45190 the shoulder straps near¦45192 where the shoulder straps join¦45193 with the sacred apron just above¦45194 the¦45195 waistband¦45195.
\v 21 They¦45198 tied¦45198 the¦45201 rings¦45202 on the sacred pouch to¦45203 the¦45205 rings¦45205 on the¦45206 sacred apron¦45206 with¦45207 a blue cord¦45207, so that the sacred pouch was¦45209 above the¦45212 waistband¦45212 and¦45214 would not¦45214 come loose from¦45218 the¦45219 apron¦45219. They did these things exactly as¦45220 Yahweh¦45222 had¦45221 instructed¦45221 Mosheh¦45225 \add <to do\add*.
\s1 Making the other clothes
\rem /s1 Additional Clothing for the Priests; Other Priestly Garments; Making the Other Priestly Garments
\r (Exo. 28:31-43)
\p
\v 22 \add @Bezalel¦45227\add* had a weaver¦45233 make¦45227 the¦45230 robe¦45230 \add that would be worn under\add* the¦45231 sacred apron¦45231 entirely¦45234 from blue \add material\add*.
\v 23 It¦45240 opened down the¦45241 middle¦45240 like¦45241 other clothes and¦45237 had a¦45242 border¦45243 around¦45245 this opening¦45237 so that it¦45247 wouldn't tear¦45247,
\v 24 and¦45249 the¦45252 bottom hem had \add decorative\add* pomegranates¦45254 on¦45250 it that were made¦45249 from blue, purple¦45256, and¦45257 scarlet¦45258 yarn.
\v 25 They¦45266 \add also\add* made¦45261 \add small\add* bells¦45262 from pure¦45264 gold¦45263 and¦45265 attached them between the pomegranates¦45270 around¦45275 the bottom of¦45273 the¦45274 robe¦45274,
\v 26 so it alternated between a bell¦45279 and¦45280 a pomegranate¦45280 going around¦45287 the¦45285 hem, just¦45289 as¦45289 Yahweh¦45291 had¦45290 instructed¦45290 Mosheh¦45294.
\p
\v 27 A weaver¦45303 made¦45297 tunics¦45300 for¦45304 Aaron¦45304 and¦45305 his¦45305 sons¦45305 from fine¦45301 linen¦45301,
\v 28 along with the¦45308 turban¦45308 and¦45307 caps from fine¦45309 linen, the underwear¦45317 made from twisted¦45320 finely-spun linen,
\v 29 and¦45322 the¦45324 waistband¦45324 from fine¦45325 linen¦45325 with blue, purple¦45328, and¦45329 scarlet¦45330 embroidery, just¦45333 as¦45333 Yahweh¦45335 had¦45334 instructed¦45334 Mosheh¦45338.
\p
\v 30 They¦45341 made¦45341 a \add decorative\add* plate¦45344 (to represent a holy crown¦45345) from pure¦45347 gold¦45348 and¦45350 they¦45341 engraved¦45353 ‘Dedicated to Yahweh¦45356’ on¦45351 it¦45351 (like you'd do for¦45356 a signet ring).
\v 31 They¦45370 put¦45358 a blue cord¦45360 on¦45359 it to attach it to the front of¦45360 the¦45365 turban¦45365, just¦45367 as¦45367 Yahweh¦45369 had¦45368 instructed¦45368 Mosheh¦45372.
\s1 Mosheh inspects the finished components
\rem /s1 The Completion of the Work; Moses Inspects the Work; The Work Completed; Moses Inspects the Tabernacle
\r (Exo. 35:10-19)
\p
\v 32 And¦45389 \add so\add* all¦45376 the¦45378 components of¦45378 the¦45379 residence¦45379, the tent¦45379 for meeting¦45381 \add <God\add*, were¦45375 finished¦45375—the Israelis¦45384 had¦45387 done just what Yahweh¦45388 had instructed¦45387 Mosheh¦45391.
\v 33 \add @The¦45399 craftsmen¦45399\add* brought¦45396 the \add disassembled\add* residence¦45399 to¦45400 Mosheh¦45402—the tent¦45399 and¦45406 all¦45408 its¦45410 equipment¦45410, the clips, the frames¦45412 with their bars¦45413, and¦45415 the pillars¦45415 with their bases¦45416,
\v 34 the reddened rams¦45422 hide tarpaulin and¦45418 the top sea-cow hide¦45421 tarpaulin, the curtain¦45430 for covering¦45426 \add <the most sacred place\add*,
\v 35 the¦45435 box¦45435 for the¦45436 transcript¦45436 slabs and¦45437 its¦45439 poles¦45439, the¦45441 atonement¦45441 platform,
\v 36 the¦45445 table¦45445 with all¦45448 its¦45450 utensils¦45450 and¦45451 the¦45452 sacred bread¦45452 to present¦45453 to God,
\v 37 the pure¦45458 lampstand¦45457 with its¦45461 row¦45463 of¦45466 lamps¦45461 and¦45464 all¦45466 its utensils¦45468 and the lamp¦45461 oil¦45470,
\v 38 the gold¦45475 \add incense\add* altar¦45474, the anointing¦45478 oil¦45477 and¦45479 the fragrant¦45481 incense¦45480, and¦45482 the curtain for the tent¦45485 entrance¦45484,
\v 39 the \add large\add* bronze¦45490 altar¦45489 with its grating¦45493, its poles¦45500, and¦45501 all¦45503 its utensils¦45505, the¦45508 washbasin¦45508 with its base¦45511,
\v 40 the¦45514 courtyard curtains¦45514 with their pillars¦45518 and¦45519 bases¦45521, the courtyard gate¦45525 curtain¦45514, \add all the\add* ropes¦45529 and¦45530 tent¦45530 pegs¦45530 and¦45531 all¦45532 the items to service¦45535 the¦45536 residence¦45536 as the¦45537 tent¦45537 of¦45537 meeting¦45538,
\v 41 and the finely-woven clothes for serving¦45544 in¦45545 the holy place¦45545, the sacred¦45549 clothes for¦45550 Aharon¦45550 the¦45551 priest¦45551, and¦45552 the¦45554 clothes for his¦45555 sons¦45555 to¦45556 \add serve as\add* priests¦45556.
\p
\v 42 The¦45568 Israelis¦45569 had done¦45567 all¦45571 the¦45573 work¦45573 just as Yahweh¦45562 had¦45561 instructed¦45561 Mosheh¦45565.
\v 43 Mosheh¦45576 \add ≈inspected\add* all¦45579 the¦45581 work¦45581, and¦45582 wow, they¦45583 had¦45583 done¦45583 it¦45584 just¦45585 as¦45585 Yahweh¦45587 had instructed¦45586 \add <them\add*, and¦45590 Mosheh blessed¦45590 them¦45591.
\c 40
\s1 Erecting the sacred tent
\rem /s1 Setting Up the Tabernacle; The Tabernacle Erected and Its Equipment Installed; The Tabernacle Completed; Setting Up and Dedicating the Tent of the Lord's Presence
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦45596 told¦45600 Mosheh¦45599,
\v 2 “On¦45609 the first day¦45602 of¦45607 the first month¦45607, you¦45608 should set¦45608 up¦45608 the¦45611 tent¦45611 \add ≈where we'll meet¦45613\add*.
\v 3 Put¦45615 the¦45618 box¦45618 for the¦45619 transcript¦45619 slabs in its place¦45615 and¦45620 \add hang\add* the curtain¦45626 to screen¦45620 it \add from sight\add*.
\v 4 Then¦45628 bring¦45628 in the¦45631 \add bread\add* table¦45631 and¦45632 arrange¦45632 its¦45635 utensils, and¦45636 bring¦45636 in the¦45639 lampstand¦45639 and¦45640 set up¦45640 the lamps¦45643,
\v 5 and¦45645 put¦45654 the gold¦45649 incense¦45650 altar¦45648 in¦45651 front¦45651 of¦45648 the sacred box¦45652 and¦45654 set¦45654 up the entrance¦45658 curtain for¦45650 the tent¦45659.
\v 6 Put¦45662 the altar¦45663 for burning¦45664 sacrifices¦45664 in¦45665 front¦45665 of¦45663 the entrance¦45666 to¦45665 the sacred¦45667 tent¦45667 \add ≈where we'll meet¦45670\add*.
\v 7 Put¦45673 the washbasin between¦45676 the¦45678 sacred¦45678 tent¦45678 and¦45680 that altar¦45681, and¦45682 fill it with water¦45684.
\v 8 \add ≈Set-up the¦45689 curtains around¦45690 the outside to make the courtyard, and¦45691 also¦45691 set up the courtyard's¦45696 entrance¦45695 curtain\add*.
\p
